{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie","id":1114985,"title":"99% Solar PCs are Muslim Kenyan Gay Atheist Commie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-12T02:10:46-07:00","id":1114985,"title":"99% Solar PCs are Muslim Kenyan Gay Atheist Commie","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/dvXO0dK.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/HgN95ZE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/wus6Ash.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <hr /><br /> Religion, belief and worship in Exalted as presented in the book felt kinda weird to me, so if you guys don't mind me asking some question.......<br /> <br /> <b>1/</b> If a Solar is the roaming Creation freely type, then most of them will become less religious as they travel, aren't they ? Since meeting other spirits will makes them realize that their God is just merely a Terrestrial sky god and not some almighty creator who birth the world in seven day (this'll happen even early for Zenith).<br /> <br /> <b>2/ </b>Is &quot;Cultural Christian&quot; a thing if you are a non-religious Solar, as in you celebrate a festival not because you believe in its backstory about a guy coming back from the dead, but more because it's your city's traditions/cultural identity and you aren't gonna stop eating those delicious cake just because the stories aren't real. Kinda like an atheist Jew who still attend Jewish holidays.<br /> <br /> <b>3/ </b>Just in my house alone are the altar for my deceased grandparent, near it is the altar for the Buddhism pantheon, scattering around the house are altars to god of kitchen, the ground, luck, wealth, longevity...etc. In the street are temples and shrines to river gods, wandering ghosts, deified people or even animal like tiger.<br /> <br /> Is this suppose to be what most the religion landscape in Creation looks like i.e People follow a mixture of different beliefs and deities from various religions ? Since I heard that Creation is suppose to be animism and Shintoism or something, does that means place like Haborhead and Whitewall are oddballs since they only worship one supreme deity ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-12-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":24}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T02:19:19-07:00","id":1114987,"title":"","content":"Before I read the subject of the post, I really need to compliment this comic, especially the two renditions of the Sun bestowing authority on the Solars. The art if some of the best it's ever been, and it made me laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T02:27:37-07:00","id":1114990,"title":"","content":"1. Honestly I think most people in Creation, from the lowest peasant to the highest king, have a practical knowledge of their gods. They worship the gods as the giver of good things if mollified and bringers of dooms if they are unhappy. And those gods they do worship tend to be ones that have a distinct impact on their lives, like a field god for a hamlet of farmers or a directional goddess of trade for a Guildsman. Anything beyond that, like the very distant Incarna or gods in general, are simply included in generic acts of reverence to make sure none of them draw offense or withdraw their blessings. In short its not an act of faith as a Christian might understand it but a divine business proposition. This is of course a generalization. Creation has plenty of dedicated cults and sects of various gods.<br /> <br /> 2. Sure. Stemming from above many people are more interested in the feast at the festivals than than the meaning behind them. I don't think the gods would even see it as a problem as long as the worship at the appropriate times and place keeps coming and a basic respect is maintained. Of course some gods are more temperamental and demanding than others so its not always a safe assumption. <br /> <br /> 3. Yes. At least in the Threshold you would see roadside shrines to a dozen gods right next to the grand temples to the Incarna, with people attending the various shrines and temples as life's needs and duties drove them. In Immaculate-held areas the worship of the gods falls more directly into the province of its monks than the common people but even there little private shrines pop up all over the place. Even Harborhead only recognizes its bull god as its patron deity but that doesn't stop worship of various other types of god as long as the populace remembers who is the patron god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T02:29:39-07:00","id":1114991,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cMost witches don\u2019t believe in gods. They know that the gods exist, of course. They even deal with them occasionally. But they don\u2019t believe in them. They know them too well. It would be like believing in the postman.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1654.Terry_Pratchett\" target=\"_blank\">Terry Pratchett</a><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/929672\" target=\"_blank\">Witches Abroad</a></span></span></span><br /> <br /> The thing is, solars are demigods. They're interaction with religion is muddied by the fact that they're <i>part of it. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T02:32:19-07:00","id":1114993,"title":"","content":"Okay, the subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie#post1114985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>1/</b> If a Solar is the roaming Creation freely type, then most of them will become less religious as they travel, aren't they ? Since meeting other spirits will makes them realize that their God is just merely a Terrestrial sky god and not some almighty creator who birth the world in seven day (this'll happen even early for Zenith).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that it depends on the nature of the Solar's initial religion. If it was based on a significant deception on the part of the god involved, particularly in the form of elevating their own significance, I would say that a lot of Solars would become disillusioned by likely experiences. If it's somebody more like Ten Sheaves, important to the community and promulgating a decent message that the Solar can still live by as one of the Exalted, then I would say one can still maintain a lot of respect for the god (in a manner that can include worship), even while being elevated to the status of a peer.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt may sometimes go further and become a case of the religious element of the gods still being held up as important while the Solar inserts themselves into it. Not necessarily as a deity, but at least a case of &quot;these are still figures to honour and principles to live by, and I'll lead you through the structure of them&quot;. That kind of what Perfect Soul is doing, although in her case her own regard for the gods is lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>2/ </b>Are &quot;Cultural Christian&quot; a thing if you are a non-religious Solar, as in you celebrate a festival not because you believe in its backstory about a guy coming back from the dead, but more because it's your city's traditions/cultural identity and you aren't gonna stop eating those delicious cake just because the stories aren't real. Kinda like an atheist Jew who still attend Jewish holidays.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh I'd say definitely. On top of ones who personally enjoy the trapping of ceremonies and festivals, I would say there are many who see them as valuable as a means for a community to express and reinforce its values, and just have a dedicated chance for socializing if much of their daily lives otherwise involves labour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>3/ </b>Just in my house alone are the altar for my deceased grandparent, near it is the altar for the Buddhism pantheon, scattering around the house are altars to god of kitchen, the ground, luck, wealth, longevity...etc. In the street are temples and shrines to river gods, wandering ghosts, deified people or even animal like tiger.<br /> <br /> Is this suppose to be what most the religion landscape in Creation looks like i.e People follow a mixture of different beliefs and deities from various religions ? Since I heard that Creation is suppose to be animism and Shintoism or something, does that means place like Haborhead and Whitewall are oddballs since they only worship one supreme deity ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThereabouts, on both counts (although I imagine that even in Harborhead, a lot of local deities have some household worship, even if they come second to Ahlat). I'd say it's most evident in cities such as Nexus, where gatherings of large numbers of people will create a synthesis of many cultural systems and practices, and knowledge of a wide variety of spirits, and Great Forks is kind of built around it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that in a lot of smaller areas, especially rural, it's easier for certain gods to monopolize the people's attention, either because they control a very significant landscape feature, or have strong-armed their way into it. If they're organized into a court, promoting a bit of secondary worship for a subordinate is likely a goal that many compete for influence over, or might receive as a reward for some service.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:56:25-07:00","id":1115011,"title":"","content":"Yeap, Jen's art always makes my day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:14:46-07:00","id":1115038,"title":"","content":"If somebody put &quot;just fucking wish for world peace, you scum sifu&quot; on a t-shirt, I might buy it. <br /> <br /> 1. If you're already accustomed to polytheism, incorporating other people's religions into your own isn't too much of a mental hurdle. Even if you're a committed monotheist, it doesn't take much in the way of mental gymnastics to accept the idea that people in other places have their own beliefs. You may think those beliefs are, to some extent, wrong (only you know the true will of God!), but you accept them anyway.<br /> <br /> Something important to remember is that the books do not have the First Commandment (&quot;Thou shalt have no other gods before me&quot;) written in them anywhere, for any deity. Unless you decide otherwise, there's no <i>rule</i> saying that you must refuse to acknowledge other gods even if you're committed to only worshiping one. <br /> <br /> 2. I believe people who practice a religion, but are not spiritual, absolutely do exist in Creation. In fact, they might be more common in Creation than in the real world - in Creation, you can personally meet your gods on occasion, and your interactions with them might be more like a series of business transactions than true worship. That, I think, would lead more people to develop pragmatic, earthly-minded approaches to the practice of religion.<br /> <br /> 3. Different parts of Creation have different practices. I suspect your house's collection of shrines makes a pretty good template for most of the world. Maybe in areas where the Immaculates hold sway, nobody is allowed to have personal shrines and access to public shrines is limited to certain days and times. Maybe in Sijan, monuments for the ancestors outnumber the temples 100-1. Maybe there are Malfean cults that eschew the worship of all gods in favor of demons. Whatever you think is appropriate!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:20:32-07:00","id":1115041,"title":"","content":"&quot;No other gods before me&quot; can also be stretched to &quot;other gods exist, but I'm better&quot; if you really want it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:53:18-07:00","id":1115053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115041#post1115041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No other gods before me&quot; can also be stretched to &quot;other gods exist, but I'm better&quot; if you really want it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>We call that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monolatrism\" target=\"_blank\">monolatrism</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:27:36-07:00","id":1115113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie#post1114985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religion, belief and worship in Exalted as presented in the book felt kinda weird to me, so if you guys don't mind me asking some question.......<br /> <br /> <b>1/</b> If a Solar is the roaming Creation freely type, then most of them will become less religious as they travel, aren't they ? Since meeting other spirits will makes them realize that their God is just merely a Terrestrial sky god and not some almighty creator who birth the world in seven day (this'll happen even early for Zenith).<br /> <br /> <b>2/ </b>Is &quot;Cultural Christian&quot; a thing if you are a non-religious Solar, as in you celebrate a festival not because you believe in its backstory about a guy coming back from the dead, but more because it's your city's traditions/cultural identity and you aren't gonna stop eating those delicious cake just because the stories aren't real. Kinda like an atheist Jew who still attend Jewish holidays.<br /> <br /> <b>3/ </b>Just in my house alone are the altar for my deceased grandparent, near it is the altar for the Buddhism pantheon, scattering around the house are altars to god of kitchen, the ground, luck, wealth, longevity...etc. In the street are temples and shrines to river gods, wandering ghosts, deified people or even animal like tiger.<br /> <br /> Is this suppose to be what most the religion landscape in Creation looks like i.e People follow a mixture of different beliefs and deities from various religions ? Since I heard that Creation is suppose to be animism and Shintoism or something, does that means place like Haborhead and Whitewall are oddballs since they only worship one supreme deity ?</div> </div> </div> </div>first I wanted to say that i loved your comic, though i never got the feeling that the sole god the solar exalted would worship would be the sun, it is reasonable to believe considering that he is the source of their power. so starting on the idea that a solar would be a worshiper of the sun let's go over your points<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>1.) </b>I think that this really depends on the character being played, especially in a setting like creation where faith and belief get a bit muddled when you can actually see the physical manifestations of gods and demons in the world around you which proves their existence. I think in creation religious practice would have a lot more to do with who you believe is going to benefit you the most, and in most cases that is not going to be the sun considering he has turned his attention away from creation, whereas of course you're going to give worship to the local field guardian, or you could starve. however, it would be very interesting to see a character whose motivation is to earn the suns respect again and to turn them back towards creation, in which case a manifestation of their religion would be their faith that they can make the sun god care again, for this character no amount of seeing other spirits is going to change their opinion on worshipping the sun, for that matter no amount of seeing other spirits is likely to change anyones already preconceived notions about faith, especially if they are an ardent believer, given that seeing spirits in creation should not be all that uncommon, although most peoples of creation imo would shift their worship as appropriate as they move from place to place recognizing the greater power of one god over that particular region than the god from the previous region.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>2.) </b>As someone who is from a minority christian ethno-religious group who was at one point agnostic, i would like to believe that a culturally religious but practically agnostic character is totally possible, and even likely. Religion tends to be for many people about what they can get out of it, and it is likely that a solar who starts to realize that they do not need outside forces to gain what they need would in the long run become less observant in their thoughts, while still maintaining cultural practices do to their importance to them and tying to their people. This of course is not going to be the case for everyone as some people maintain faiths for other reasons that don't rely on the personal benefit one can attain, but the quote from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> really characterizes for me what i think many exalted would eventually grow to feel:</div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1114991#post1114991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cMost witches don\u2019t believe in gods. They know that the gods exist, of course. They even deal with them occasionally. But they don\u2019t believe in them. They know them too well. It would be like believing in the postman.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1654.Terry_Pratchett\" target=\"_blank\">Terry Pratchett</a><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/929672\" target=\"_blank\">Witches Abroad</a></span></span></span> The thing is, solars are demigods. They're interaction with religion is muddied by the fact that they're <i>part of it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Thinking about exalted and faith gives me a lot of ideas for an exalted who is the last of their ethno-religious group and trying to revive their dead god by creating a kingdom that mimics their long dead home.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">That said, I would also love to see an example of a long dead religion whose devout practitioners all died out millenia ago but its cultural practices are maintained by the exalted who is the last remaining member of their ethno-religious group.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>3.)</b>The thing with the exalted religious setting is that it mixes in aspects from a lot of religions, like Shintoism for example with the animistic nature of creation's god's, or Buddhism with its enlightenment and reincarnation, the immaculate faith is very similar to the concept of hinduism in which a person reincarnates many times until attaining the ultimate form, even the abrahamic faiths get a mention with the concepts of divine saviors as well as many other aspects of faiths from many other religions, all of which can be expected to have a direct pay off as these things actually have visible effect in creation where as we in our world have to go off of faith. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For how this will look for the most part, except for the oddballs you mentioned, is that i belive it will function very much like religion does in japan, where for the longest time the only faith was shintoism, but then the emperor's family, who is supposed to be the direct descendets of the sun deity amaterasu, became buddhists during the heian period requiring the need for an interpretation of faith tat could include both realities, something that many christian japanese also do in incorporating all three faiths into their daily practices.</div> <br /> <br /> By all of this i mean that i think faith in exalted would be much more like a make your own combo rather than selecting from a set menu, and that a persons actual adherence/ faith to that combo that they or their region has made will depend greatly on that person themselves and how they interact with the new information presented to them. in some cases like a solar who grew up in the immaculate faith this could result in some problems that will be solved either will reverting to full agnosticism, or maybe just a small adjustment in their faith.<br /> Although i would love to play the latter character as someone who is constantly making small adjustments to my personal version of my faith based on conversations with people from my own religion and different one's about how they view faith, ultimately i think both characters are very interesting concepts that depend on how you develop the character or npc from the beginning.<br /> The current character i play grew up in the house of their goddess mother their entire life and is currently trying to resurrect them after their apparent death, but they aren't particularly religious at all and they also find the prospect of people worshiping them uncomfortable, and even though this is completely different than what i just said id be interested in playing its how the character ended up by developing his personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:57:10-07:00","id":1115139,"title":"","content":"All I can really add (that was a very amusing comic, and the art is great even by Jen standards) is that I have more than a few Solars who'd at least pay respect at a temple to a god. Maybe less out of religious worship and more an intention to be <i>polite</i>.<br /> <br /> Granted, those same Solars probably wouldn't pray for world peace, and would likely take the stance of &quot;Praying is all well and good, but we have the power to make things better&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:02:23-07:00","id":1115142,"title":"","content":"Her ahoge has retracted - the matter is grave indeed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:04:27-07:00","id":1115143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1114991#post1114991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, solars are demigods. They're interaction with religion is muddied by the fact that they're <i>part of it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Greek heroes are demigod too and people seems to treat them more like a famous person than the children of Zeus, though they are weaker than Solar and also get screwed over by the gods most of the time so it's probably a bad comparison.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1114993#post1114993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that in a lot of smaller areas, especially rural, it's easier for certain gods to monopolize the people's attention, either because they control a very significant landscape feature, or have strong-armed their way into it. If they're organized into a court, promoting a bit of secondary worship for a subordinate is likely a goal that many compete for influence over, or might receive as a reward for some service.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if gods who does this kind of thing prefer to present themselves like the Christian's God i.e They create and control everything, since it prevent people from asking question like &quot;Where does lightning come from ?&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115113#post1115113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> first I wanted to say that i loved your comic, though i never got the feeling that the sole god the solar exalted would worship would be the sun, it is reasonable to believe considering that he is the source of their power. so starting on the idea that a solar would be a worshiper of the sun let's go over your points</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Solar in the Castebook who travel around seems to be very fond of the Sun, some even calls him father. So it seems to me like Solar can become the Sun's worshiper pretty quickly, I mean, I certainly would if I see his glorious abs...........<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:44:53-07:00","id":1115163,"title":"","content":"Hey Jen, I just want to say that your artwork has really been improving, especially in your use of paneling and overall design. The first page of your comic is really impressive, and I think so far probably the best thing you've drawn. You managed to get all of the characters, expressions and bodies drawn out very well. Really, I always value your posts and the work that you put into your drawings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:51:55-07:00","id":1115168,"title":"","content":"Generally gods are like a sponsorship. Also Zeniths, who are all priests, have the endorsement of the chief god. butthey are not demanded to be exclusive. Recall even as chief Sol reigns with 7 equivalents. His holiest and most spectacular act, the eclispe is about unity/harmony with all the cycles and aspects of Creation. Solars can easily still worship their old god AND view the sun as their godfathor or patron or new paron. Each Solar has different thoughts on this.<br /> They can be dismissive but Zeniths are priests not just as sermonizers but intercesors between man and the divine. Very brutally in fact. Recall the gods and elementals compete by nature and in addition to that corruptly demand specific worship other &quot;protection rackets&quot; or did. First and then 2nd edition over here<br /> <br /> I take it thse comics are a semi regularly thing with the kind of squashy bara-ish Solars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:43:36-07:00","id":1115197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115143#post1115143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if gods who does this kind of thing prefer to present themselves like the Christian's God i.e They create and control everything, since it prevent people from asking question like &quot;Where does lightning come from ?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that can work in a <i>very</i> isolated community that is quite dependent on something that the god controls, but otherwise a spirit who would try such a thing is flying a bit too close to the sun.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think if you want to prevent people from worshipping gods that are much bigger than you, and sufficiently far away, you're better off cultivating a sense of dread around them. Don't pray to the lightning gods, it just makes them angry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:32:17-07:00","id":1115260,"title":"","content":"Hm. <br /> So, I like making religion a <i>thing</i> in my games, that seperates or unites culture groups etc. Almost more than politics. So a few thoughts. <br /> Zeniths at the end bc they make things a tad complicated.<br /> <br /> 1) Most gods worshipped probably aren't creator gods. Cosmogny is important in world religions but...Well, Zeus didn't make the world. Amaterasu to my understanding didn't either. Neither did Thor (Okay, Odin was chief god there, but 'made the world out of a dead dude' isn't high on his deeds), etc. Most gods worshiped are for either their daily involvement and actions. More common might be gods who established social orders and customs among people. Lawgivers, if you will. <br /> This is why Hearth gods are weirdly important, even if they do less asskicking compared to the big names. They protect and govern the home, which often reflects the cosmos. Hestia doesn't do much, but she doesn't need to. She's in charge of domestic affairs.<br /> And as others have said, most faiths, regardless of size, easily adapt to incorporate other gods into them in some form. Even 'monotheists' have the demon/saint label they can place on things. The bigger trick with Monotheistic Creator God is the whole Almighty part. That gets tricky when you get beaten up. But again, that's not exactly a common god type.<br /> <br /> 2)Cutlural Christian is probably a thing. in the Ancient times it was as well. People knew ritual had value on it's own, regardless of reality. A bigger point however is that there isn't a religion so widespread as Christianity or Islam except the Immaculate Order. So Religion and political/ethnic group will probably get blended to some degree.<br /> Not to say national variations on those religions aren't a thing, but not typically as blatant and tend to get invovled in that Saints buisness.<br /> <br /> 3)Yes? I mean, Creations landscape of religion probably varies greatly, and might not be as apparently clean cut as sometimes real world religions are. Gods migth move, but then their context will probably change as well. Indra's role in Hinduism, from what I've read, varies a bit depending on the time and text. A more concrete example might be how the Roman and Greeks in popular conception share deities but change the roles to better reflect certain values of their culture (you could argue this about all Indo-European affairs, but my knowledge gets muddy).<br /> <br /> Zeniths throw a giant wrench into this because they <i>see</i> the King of the Gods. And he <i>talks</i> to them. ...Which I like.<br /> What a Zenith takes away from that experience probably depends on their standing and beliefs. After all, my shaman saw the UCS as the elephant god Hathi he had worshiped for years (the UCS just had elephant heads). The message UCS gave also will shape that, since unless it invalidates existing beliefs no reason to bother. It gets tricky if your original god claimed to be supreme...but then most gods who claimed to be supreme will also probably try to claim the vision was from them (it's short and you don't get regular contact after all). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:35:51-07:00","id":1115261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115143#post1115143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if gods who does this kind of thing prefer to present themselves like the Christian's God i.e They create and control everything, since it prevent people from asking question like &quot;Where does lightning come from ?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that many Terrestrial Gods what rein over one region try to keep it focused. You might not have one singular God saying &quot;YES, HUMANS! I CONTROL EVERYTHING! THE SUN, THE MOON, AND THE STARS ALL DANCE TO MY WILL!&quot; because there's a chance that rumors of that could reach the ears of say, a different God, some kind of Elemental, a Priest who knows these things...<br /> <br /> And let's be honest, as out of the daily affairs of Creation as the Sun stays, I wager that if he heard SOME little upstart forest god is trying to claim overship and control of the Sun, well... That's ASKING for a beam of Holy Fire to descend from on-high.<br /> <br /> Not that a god might not try to make that claim, but they'd have to be PRETTY egotistical and their territory would have to be pretty isolated for them to think it has a chance of working.<br /> <br /> Ahlat, for example, doesn't really claim to be more than he is. It's just that what he is is a VERY powerful god who controls cattle and war for an entire Direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:50:53-07:00","id":1115265,"title":"","content":"Jesus, Jen, your art just gets better and better.<br /> A word regarding cultural and religious identity: I'm Christian, Southern Baptist technically (one of the more conservative denominations). I go to a Chinese church. On the week of Qingming, the service was practically empty because everyone had gone to visit the graves of their families. I would have gone too if my ancestors were on the same continent. We went not because cleaning their graves would help the dead rest in peace, but because we're Chinese, and this is what Chinese people do.<br /> Now, Creation doesn't really have a religion that's meant to be multi-ethnic like Christianity is. I guess worship of the Sun might qualify, but I don't actually remember that much direct worship of Sol (there must be some, for Perfect Soul to have knocked over his shrine, but wasn't it overgrown and abandoned?). Most directly worshipped gods are a regional thing; the god of war probably doesn't care about you, but the god of southern war and cattle raiding knows what your life is like.<br /> Actually, I guess the Maidens are pretty widely worshipped, since all Creation shares the same astrology system. But gain, I don't think anyone really worships them, just acknowledges that they exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T15:15:41-07:00","id":1115271,"title":"","content":"First off, let me join the choir of people complimenting you - hilarious comic, and very nice art! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115143#post1115143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greek heroes are demigod too and people seems to treat them more like a famous person than the children of Zeus, though they are weaker than Solar and also get screwed over by the gods most of the time so it's probably a bad comparison.....</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Well, my view on the matter is this: most people, influenced by the Cult of the Immaculate Dragons, know about Anathema, i.e. people possessed by evil spirits. They've always identified them primarily with Lunars, but now that the Solars are back of course they're Anathema too according to the Realm, and the Realm can be persuasive and culturally very wide-reaching. So people will often know to run away and seek an Immaculate Monk or Dragon-Blood as soon as they meet anyone starting to give off silver or golden light or displaying some strange mark on their brow. Of course the fact that the Abyssals have visible animas and caste marks as well doesn't help the Solars and Lunars, because the Abyssals actually are usually hostile to Creation.<br /> <br /> So people are very confused. But they mostly <i>fear</i> the Celestial Exalted. Not many know that the Solars are the Chosen of the Unconquered Sun. It doesn't help that the Unconquered Sun is not doing his job - he's completely absorbed in the Games of Divinity and only a substitutive bureau of minor Celestial gods is charged with answering prayers directed to him. They try to, but these &quot;letters to Santa&quot; are legion, and sometimes they give off a random miracle without reading them, or smite the worshippers to discourage further praying (and further headaches for them).<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is rarely worshipped, as a result, and his temples are mostly ruins (when they're not imperishable manses). Common people are more likely to pray to the god of the nearby river, to the gods of the fields they work in, to the god of the road they use most, to the god of the village/town they reside in. Sometimes they hold sacred hunts in Luna's honor (she's not as completely absent as Sol, but then again, she's awesome like that), but they mostly worship the small gods ruling in the area they live in, and some celestial gods presiding over matters currently important to them (a Southern cattle raider or soldier prays to Alaht, a slaver to Rabszolga, and so on). Then there are the little gods you wish to avoid, like the sirens, who try to have sex with you and/or eat you. The &quot;sex&quot; part is not usually the problem, you see.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> That's it more or less regarding the gods. Also, people know they can be morally bankrupt and favorably disposed towards bribes, but they're gods, so the best course of action is to acquiesce to their demands and <i>perhaps</i> hope a hero passes by and teaches them a lesson. If that hero is an Anathema, well, they helped, so they can't be all that bad, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115143#post1115143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if gods who does this kind of thing prefer to present themselves like the Christian's God i.e They create and control everything, since it prevent people from asking question like &quot;Where does lightning come from ?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not normally. AFAIK gods don't really go for lying to their worshippers. Racketeering, yes, lying, not so much - most of all not such huge lies. Yes, even little gods are powerful compared to mortals, but no field god would ever pretend they created the world. The field is clearly posterior to the creation of... Creation. And no one would believe them.<br /> <br /> When they ask where lightning comes from they might be told some folktale more or less based in truth (air elementals, IIRC), but if they ask who created the world they'll never get the straight dope. Most people would invent something relating to the Celestial Incarnae (Unconquered Sun, Luna, the Five Maidens, very probably adding Gaia without knowing she's actually a Primordial).<br /> <br /> Those who can read and find some rather rare books might come to know Creation was shaped by the Primordials, who were asses and thus the gods created the Exalted to kill and imprison them and so on. Some of those books are spread around by the Yozis themselves, and make them appear as poor victims betrayed by their beloved creatures (shyeah right), and some savants who find those books become Yozi cultists and summon demons and work towards a Judgement Day when the Yozis will finally be freed and fix everything that's broken with the world (hahahah, sure).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115143#post1115143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Solar in the Castebook who travel around seems to be very fond of the Sun, some even calls him father. So it seems to me like Solar can become the Sun's worshiper pretty quickly, I mean, I certainly would if I see his glorious abs...........</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, their Solar Exaltations change their lives, so they tend to look favorably towards Sol. The Zeniths even receive a message from him, which inspires them and often ensures their loyalty. But not all Solars really do care about Unconquered Sun - after all, it's not like he actually chose them, in most cases. It's the Exaltation that chooses you, not the god who imbued it with their own power. So you don't actually owe anything to Sol (even though, again, Zeniths might have different experiences. Lunars too, since Luna appears to each of her Chosen. But as I was saying, she's totally rad).<br /> <br /> As for His Glorious Abs, get in line, hon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T15:41:44-07:00","id":1115279,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13651_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13651\" data-vbnamecard=\"13651\">Roswynn</a>: Actually, Solars have always been Anathema in Immaculate doctrine; since they never <i>fully</i> disappeared (only <i>mostly</i>), the Immaculates have been demonizing them as well as the Lunars.<br /> <br /> Not that it takes a thousand years of Immaculate doctrine for people to be afraid of Solars. The power they wield is scary, especially considering how messed-up humans can be.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, I wouldn't phrase it like that, namely because I doubt particular Abyssals want to destroy Creation in this edition. Are they resplendent with the powers of death and the Underworld? Yes. Does that make them &quot;hostile to Creation?&quot; Not notably more so than Solars, no.<br /> <br /> Likewise on the notion of the Sun &quot;not doing his job.&quot; Answering prayers is not the job of the gods. In fact, it's generally a sign of dereliction of their duty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T17:39:27-07:00","id":1115312,"title":"","content":"Underworld agents presence reads hostile their essence radia<br /> tes more frely and <br /> Abyssals either bring ruin and decay or dres like pure evil to avoid bringin the dark omens and horrors.<br /> <br /> Certainly relations to the Underworld will be complex, there is a person there a d much much more communicaive and trustworthy and ersonal than the field god or even the Exaled. its how the Slver Prince did his thing.<br /> But the Assals are rather obviously death bringers if you see them. Also their big debut was Thorns castin them primarily as murders and invaders on the back of a corpse giant. Maybe they are friendly, in the end, but their first impression is very very naurally bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:10:33-07:00","id":1115373,"title":"","content":"Always remember that in Creation the gods are real, the gods are multiple, and none of them claim to be the One True God (unless the god has gone insane). There is not and never has been the concept of One True God in Creation. In short, <i>\u200bCreation is polytheistic</i>. This is an absolute fact, as solid and provable in Creation as the existence of solid objects in our world. To people from Creation, the movie The Ten Commandments would be unspeakably weird. The original would make a lot more sense, back when the Israelites weren't monotheistic and the Plagues were basically the god of Israel duelling with the gods of Egypt. The god of Israel sends plagues, the gods of Egypt harden Pharaohs' heart. Repeat until the gods of Egypt decide it's not a fight worth winning. What's the good of wiping out the Israelites if their own worshippers get wiped out in the process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:15:04-07:00","id":1115374,"title":"","content":"That's an oversimplification of things. I'm absolutely certain there are plenty of divinities in Creation which claim to be the only true divinity. There's also probably plenty of people and Exalts doing the same.<br /> <br /> It's not like the Celestial Bureaucracy gives these people a stamp or verification, and other gods have more important things to do than correct the beliefs of people whose beliefs would not necessarily be changed by the presence of other beings.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, being worshipped or received as a god is not a certainty related to taxonomy and has more to do with context and reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:50:01-07:00","id":1115388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115279#post1115279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13651_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13651\" data-vbnamecard=\"13651\">Roswynn</a>: Actually, Solars have always been Anathema in Immaculate doctrine; since they never <i>fully</i> disappeared (only <i>mostly</i>), the Immaculates have been demonizing them as well as the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115279#post1115279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Abyssals, I wouldn't phrase it like that, namely because I doubt particular Abyssals want to destroy Creation in this edition. Are they resplendent with the powers of death and the Underworld? Yes. Does that make them &quot;hostile to Creation?&quot; Not notably more so than Solars, no<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Abyssals directly serve beings who have been charged with killing Creation. Sure, Deathlords procrastinate a lot, and it's not like they can snap their fingers and just make it happen. But Solars <i>usually</i> don't lead the legions of the dead against the living or try to expand Shadowlands, for instance, while Deathknights are ordered to commit a whole range of heinous crimes against mortals. Sure, not all obey. But I really don't see them, as a whole, as a benevolent, positive force in Creation. The fact they're all &quot;chivalrous&quot; only means they murder <i>slightly fewer</i> innocent people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115279#post1115279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise on the notion of the Sun &quot;not doing his job.&quot; Answering prayers is not the job of the gods. In fact, it's generally a sign of dereliction of their duty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're actually in the right on this. Gods should usually bless only specific rituals if anything and are otherwise restricted to making sure their aspect of Creation prospers, and when they establish rackets in which they are to be placated with prayer and sacrifice if they're to spare their worshippers it's a highly illegal practice, of course, and rightly so. Still, Sol's duty is to protect Creation, and he's just not doing it (with the exception of trying to steer some Zeniths on the right track with a few cryptic words). He did nothing when the Deathlords unleashed the Contagion and the Fair Folk invaded. He barely even has time left to sometimes fly the Daystar, mostly leaving Nysela to do the job. He's almost completely taken by the Games. Answering prayers is not the job of the gods, you're right, but Unconquered Sun is neglecting his duties far worse than many gods who <i>do</i> answer prayers. I'm not blaming him period, the Games are the Games, but Luna, for instance, manages to find the time to at least partially fulfill her obligations. Sol's perfection is damaged by his addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:05:17-07:00","id":1115392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Abyssals directly serve beings who have been charged with killing Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Are</i> they?<br /> <br /> The 3e Core treats Deathlords as something rather more enigmatic than the simplistic campaign-end-bosses they were for 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solars <i>usually</i> don't lead the legions of the dead against the living or try to expand Shadowlands, for instance, while Deathknights are ordered to commit a whole range of heinous crimes against mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, we've got something of a cleaner slate this time 'round. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I really don't see them, as a whole, as a benevolent, positive force in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say they were benevolent? I'll happily acknowledge that none of the characters I've played would want a Deathlord or Abyssal as their next-door neighbor, but that hardly makes them intrinsically opposed to Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, Sol's duty is to protect Creation\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was the job he was given by the Primordials - if you'll recall, he gave them three hundred rather spectacular letters of resignation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He did nothing when the Deathlords unleashed the Contagion and the Fair Folk invaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he stepped in and intervened, would he not be undermining the very Mandate of Heaven he gave to the Exalted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115388#post1115388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026but Unconquered Sun is neglecting his duties far worse than many gods who <i>do</i> answer prayers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the duties of a king?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-13-2017, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:45:31-07:00","id":1115398,"title":"","content":"Alucard, I can't make heads or tails of the Abyssals' short blurb in the core book. I'm basing my facts on what we've always known to be true for 2 editions and 16 years. It might be that this edition disproves it and Abyssals are a whole different beasts, crap, perhaps they've become all nice people all of a sudden, but I'm not a big fan of pet theories.<br /> <br /> As for Sol, he loves Creation and it's his Nature to defend it from &quot;all threats to the natural order&quot;. He was just too addicted to intervene. Sure, Mandate of Heaven and all that, and during the 1st Age he could've played the Games in peace, since his Chosen were actually alive and ruling the world somewhat competently. But the Contagion and the subsequent Fair Folk invasion? Did he expect the remaining Exalted to protect Creation? What if the Scarlet Empress hadn't managed to wrest control of the Realm Defense Grid?<br /> <br /> The duties of a king are to protect his people and his lands, to keep the peace, to promote justice and prosperity. Only the worst rulers ignore their duties to their subjects. Only a tyrant feels no duty at all, and we know that Unconquered Sun is many things, but not a tyrant. Again, sure, the Games, but the net result is <i>still</i> that he ain't doing his job. If he were, he wouldn't need an office of minor deities to address the prayers directed to <i>him</i>. Luna doesn't have such an office. Alaht, Rabszolga, Burning Feather, Nara-O... he's the only one who needs help in that area, <i>and he's letting Nysela fly the Daystar</i><i> alone</i>. Think about it - the god of the sun is actually almost never found anywhere near the sun! If that ain't neglecting your duties, hell, the meaning of words must have changed while I wasn't paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:51:31-07:00","id":1115400,"title":"","content":"1). Well the big thing to keep in mind is that the closest thing to the relationship the people of creation have with their gods that we see IRL is the shinto-model where they're closer to local lords than ultimate authorities on anything. One of the defining religions of Creation boils down to 'Don't worship the gods too much, it gives them ideas above their station.'<br /> <br /> The vast majority of gods are gods of things like the local river or such, and rare is the spirit willing to claim power on the level of the Incarnae even as a bluff or a prank. Most exalted with a bit of occult study are more than capable of dealing with uppity gods.<br /> <br /> In fact look at the ability list, there's no knowledge religion like in some other games, because gods aren't special, they fall under occult like ghosts, elementals, and other spirits. They have desires, follies, and the vast majority aren't all that powerful, especially outside their specific domains.<br /> <br /> So it's not even a solar thing really, most people aren't going to go praying to a god for world peace, because that's outside the wheel house of all but the top tier divinities who haven't been really active recently.<br /> <br /> Conversely Atheism is the wrong word. Atheism implies a disbelief in divinities, which in creation is probably a lot like not believing in Skitter if you live in brockton bay.<br /> <br /> All that said exaltation, especially once you pick up the ability to find and affect dematerialized spirits, alters the power balance between a person and the gods, it's not that the person believes in gods any less, it's that they're now the more powerful party and the gods can't pull that disappearing trick they do to hide from people against you. Furthermore the exalt is empowered with their own divine powers and are thus able to perform feats of their own, in many cases an exalt can quickly grow to be better at whatever service the local gods provide, and alter the relationship between the humans and the local divinities.<br /> <br /> So it's not that Solars become atheistic, it's that in a world with a fairly mercenary take on the relationship between mortals and gods, Solars are the nations with well trained citizen armies.<br /> <br /> 2.) Probably, in fact you'll probably find most people are more than willing to celebrate whatever local festival is happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 07-13-2017, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:52:38-07:00","id":1115401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115374#post1115374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an oversimplification of things. I'm absolutely certain there are plenty of divinities in Creation which claim to be the only true divinity. There's also probably plenty of people and Exalts doing the same.<br /> <br /> It's not like the Celestial Bureaucracy gives these people a stamp or verification, and other gods have more important things to do than correct the beliefs of people whose beliefs would not necessarily be changed by the presence of other beings.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, being worshipped or received as a god is not a certainty related to taxonomy and has more to do with context and reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Celestial Bureaucracy, I reckon, would send Fate Ninjas to deal with any god stupid enough to claim they were the only one true god. As for Exalts, yes, sometimes they develop cults, that doesn't mean they declare themselves as the only actual deities. It would be silly - anyone can go chop some wood and meet a dryad. Deities are everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:55:27-07:00","id":1115403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115271#post1115271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, their Solar Exaltations change their lives, so they tend to look favorably towards Sol. The Zeniths even receive a message from him, which inspires them and often ensures their loyalty. But not all Solars really do care about Unconquered Sun - after all, it's not like he actually chose them, in most cases. It's the Exaltation that chooses you, not the god who imbued it with their own power. So you don't actually owe anything to Sol (even though, again, Zeniths might have different experiences. Lunars too, since Luna appears to each of her Chosen. But as I was saying, she's totally rad).</div> </div> </div> </div>He seems to choose all of the Solars in Castebook though, there is even one Dawn slave on the Blessed Isle who keeps getting dreams of freedom from the Sun which is kinda hard to happen if he don't care who get exalted as his chosen.<br /> <br /> And I think that Ex3 follow this mode rather than the &quot;Automatic flying shard&quot; in Ex2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T23:20:26-07:00","id":1115405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115401#post1115401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Bureaucracy, I reckon, would send Fate Ninjas to deal with any god stupid enough to claim they were the only one true god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you really think they'd do that? Why the hell would they care? Hypothetically speaking if they were to respond, it would be because that god is getting worship at all. The dirty secret of the Celestial Bureaucracy is that they're not supposed to do that stuff at all. But no, they would not respond because some god somewhere or other told some unimportant people who will die in the wink of an eye that they're the only true divinity.<br /> <br /> Ratanga, God of the kita tribes tells them he is the only real god. Unless he actually does something worthy of the attention of the Bureau of Destiny or Fakharu gets off his ass and does his job as Censor (preventing Ratanga from getting worship AT ALL) then nobody is gonna go and stop him. There are a billion things more important than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115401#post1115401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Exalts, yes, sometimes they develop cults, that doesn't mean they declare themselves as the only actual deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Do you think that every thing or person that declares themselves a god is a capital G God of the Celestial Bureaucracy? God is just a word, demons, elementals, the dead, mortals, Exalts and other creatures can and will regularly claim that word to describe themselves, and people will accord them worship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115401#post1115401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be silly - anyone can go chop some wood and meet a dryad. Deities are everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you and other people would benefit from reading and re-reading &quot;Through Mortal Eyes&quot; on page 62 of the Exalted Third Edition corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T23:32:48-07:00","id":1115406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard, I can't make heads or tails of the Abyssals' short blurb in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also lots of discussion on the subject by John and Holden and Stephen and Eric and Vance on these very forums, as well as the preview PDF they wrote up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basing my facts on what we've always known to be true for 2 editions and 16 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall that the notion of the Neverborn being connected to the Deathlords in <i>any</i> way wasn't introduced until the Abyssals fatsplat, well into the gameline. Prior to that, the Deathlords were just really powerful ghosts, and the 1e Core went so far as to indicate that there may be hundreds of them.<br /> <br /> Things change over editions, which is why we keep getting new ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be that this edition disproves it and Abyssals are a whole different beasts\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>The first set of Ex3 devs made their intentions on the matter very clear. The Deathlords are not 13 cookie-cutter Skeletors, so the Abyssals are not an existential threat to the world\u2026 or at least, not more so than the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026crap, perhaps they've become all nice people all of a sudden, but I'm not a big fan of pet theories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it's not intentional on your part, but it feels like you're trying to make my argument something it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Sol, he loves Creation and it's his Nature to defend it from &quot;all threats to the natural order&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natures weren't a trait in 2e, and I don't recall them statting him in 1e. Moreover, that would make his part in the Primordial War pretty hypocritical, would it not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, Mandate of Heaven and all that\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel you're giving this the consideration it deserves. He gave Creation to the Exalted, which by necessity includes responsibility for its well-being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did he expect the remaining Exalted to protect Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, they did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Scarlet Empress hadn't managed to wrest control of the Realm Defense Grid?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;There's always an ending.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The duties of a king are to protect his people and his lands, to keep the peace, to promote justice and prosperity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that's what the Queen of England is doing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a tyrant feels no duty at all, and we know that Unconquered Sun is many things, but not a tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, he fits at least one of the definitions of &quot;tyrant&quot; precisely.<br /> <br /> (&quot;A ruler who seized power without legal right.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he were, he wouldn't need an office of minor deities to address the prayers directed to <i>him</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much every management position requires delegating. Also, I don't care for that 2e-ism of the Sun having someone tend to his prayers, since that seems to indicate that people are praying to the Sun. Why would his temples be in such a sorry state when he has active worshippers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115398#post1115398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about it - the god of the sun is actually almost never found anywhere near the sun!</div> </div> </div> </div>The river-god is not the river, why should the sun-god have to be?<br /> <br /> (Hell, among Celestial gods, the Ocean Father is viewed as something of a weirdo for spending so much of his time in Creation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-13-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T03:27:28-07:00","id":1115455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115405#post1115405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you really think they'd do that? Why the hell would they care? Hypothetically speaking if they were to respond, it would be because that god is getting worship at all. The dirty secret of the Celestial Bureaucracy is that they're not supposed to do that stuff at all. But no, they would not respond because some god somewhere or other told some unimportant people who will die in the wink of an eye that they're the only true divinity.<br /> <br /> Ratanga, God of the kita tribes tells them he is the only real god. Unless he actually does something worthy of the attention of the Bureau of Destiny or Fakharu gets off his ass and does his job as Censor (preventing Ratanga from getting worship AT ALL) then nobody is gonna go and stop him. There are a billion things more important than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't find Ratanga. Where to?<br /> <br /> I'm still skeptic that &quot;lots&quot; of gods take this approach. The more gods/priests/Immaculate monks/savants in the area, the less successful it's gonna be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115405#post1115405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Do you think that every thing or person that declares themselves a god is a capital G God of the Celestial Bureaucracy? God is just a word, demons, elementals, the dead, mortals, Exalts and other creatures can and will regularly claim that word to describe themselves, and people will accord them worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, any supernatural being could describe themselves/be thought of as a god. I don't buy that they will &quot;regularly&quot; claim that word to describe themselves. Even less that they will say &quot;they're the One True God&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115405#post1115405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you and other people would benefit from reading and re-reading &quot;Through Mortal Eyes&quot; on page 62 of the Exalted Third Edition corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was reading it just the other day, for the umpteenth time, believe it or not. Of course people tend to conflate weird supernatural beings with the word &quot;god&quot;. <i>A god</i>, not <i>the One True God</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, don't suppose to know what I've read and what I haven't, please, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:27:00-07:00","id":1115502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also lots of discussion on the subject by John and Holden and Stephen and Eric and Vance on these very forums, as well as the preview PDF they wrote up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm new here, if you hadn't noticed. I'm not well-versed in what direction the devs will take any aspect of Creation in the books. It would be slightly disingenuous to assume anyone knows what Holden, Morke, Vance or Minton have teased in posts on a forum, or that a preview PDF even exists. BTW, if you'd point me to this preview PDF i'd be grateful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall that the notion of the Neverborn being connected to the Deathlords in <i>any</i> way wasn't introduced until the Abyssals fatsplat, well into the gameline. Prior to that, the Deathlords were just really powerful ghosts, and the 1e Core went so far as to indicate that there may be hundreds of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was <i>2003</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things change over editions, which is why we keep getting new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>one</i> reason... among <i>many</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first set of Ex3 devs made their intentions on the matter very clear. The Deathlords are not 13 cookie-cutter Skeletors, so the Abyssals are not an existential threat to the world\u2026 or at least, not more so than the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly didn't know. I've never seen them as &quot;13 cookie-cutter Skeletors&quot; though. Mask of Winters doesn't seem to have changed, BTW, nor has the Silver Prince (who might be the least villainous, perhaps, though definitely not a nice guy - &quot;Life is just preparation for death&quot; yadda yadda). The Lover Clad in Raiments of Tears binds souls, stopping them from reincarnating or passing into the Underworld, and these &quot;Loveless&quot; look for living lovers they drain of vitality, and if they go too long w/o sex they become feral cannibals. Not an existential threat to the world, but not really nice either.<br /> <br /> (BTW, even assuming a living lover would agree, and why not, this is Creation, one would think that most people, while having sex, would want to stop if they felt their vitality being drained by their ghostly lover. If the ghost doesn't stop, that's <i>rape</i>. I'll let you ponder that).<br /> <br /> Also, Ghost Steel must come from somewhere. I remember it was partly Labyrinth's ore, and partly souls of the dead. Exploiting the dead like this and in the process obliterating them forever doesn't seem all that cute.<br /> <br /> Anyways I was re-reading the Abyssal blurb.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>When the Abyssals ride forth from their bleak citadels, it is most often as agents of the Deathlords. Most of the Abyssals have sworn fealty to one of these dark lords of the Underworld, and in turn have been raised high in their master\u2019s ranks\u2014armed and armored in grim wonders, given estates in the shadowlands, and tutored in the mastery of death\u2019s black miracles. <br /> Other Abyssals forsake this master-apprentice relationship, riding alone and following their heart\u2019s urgings</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you're right, not all Abyssals serve Deathlords apparently. Those who do... well, depends on the Deathlord, I guess.<br /> <br /> For instance, the siege of Thorns:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>The Dragon-Blooded of the Thorns garrison rode forth to confront the Deathlord\u2019s forces, only to be cut down in the space of an hour by the Abyssal Exalted who emerged from the corpse-fortress\u2019s shadow. This was Creation\u2019s first introduction to Death\u2019s Lawgivers.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters could have conquered the city that same day: Juggernaut could have easily pulled down the walls, and the Abyssal Exalted gone reaving through the streets. Instead he settled in to siege. He sent rats to eat the city\u2019s food, and sickness to taint its air. As the people starved, he released pigs into the streets; the skeletons of those who ate of their cursed flesh tore their way out from the screaming bodies encasing them. In the end, he made the people of Thorns open their own gates and invite him inside. He made them beg him to deliver them from the horrors he had brought.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters was glad to oblige. Thorns is now the center of a new, swiftly-growing shadowland, and the capital of the Deathlord\u2019s nascent empire. His cold, hungry eyes now settle upon the River Province to the north</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Paints a pretty picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope it's not intentional on your part, but it feels like you're trying to make my argument something it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called sarcasm. And I really am no fan of pet theories. For now, the Abyssals don't seem to have changed much. They're still necromancers, mostly servants of mostly villainous Deathlords, and &quot;<i>Many Abyssals see only death in death, and are pleased by cruelty and blood</i>&quot; (Ex3, p.42), plus &quot;<i>Classically trained Abyssals are given a code, which speaks to the truth of the grave. This truth is instinctive, and <b>resonates even in those deathknights who forsake the Deathlords</b> </i>(bold mine)<i> to walk alone. Despair, futility, hopelessness in heroes and leaders and the hearts of men spread the Essence of the grave far more effectively than wholesale slaughter, which tends to renew vows of perseverance, survival, and commitment to the gods. Kill a wife and spare the husband, and you may have made an enemy for life, but you have also made the man questionable to everyone around him forevermore. And so the Abyssals sometimes stay their hands. They let their enemies live. They preach bleak sermons and move on without incident. They let the world move in its own course, touched by their darkness. This is the chivalry of death</i>&quot; (again, Ex3, p.42).<br /> <br /> So, yeah... yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Natures weren't a trait in 2e, and I don't recall them statting him in 1e. Moreover, that would make his part in the Primordial War pretty hypocritical, would it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, why? But you're right, I was confusing editions - it's his Motivation in Glories of the Most High.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;There's always an ending.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what, the Unconquered Sun would philosophically watch as Creation burns, because everything must eventually die? That's against everything I know about him. But if you're saying, through all these posts, that all I know of Creation from 1st and 2nd edition is suddenly no longer valid because Morke and Holden, who aren't even working on this project anymore, have written some hints teasing that they wanted some things to appear in a different light or be changed, well, I'll just play using this edition's much improved system in a mostly 2nd edition Creation. I'm not giving up a setting I know for one that won't be complete until who-knows-when, with only blurbs and teases telling me how the new devs want me to reset my knowledge. No, thanks. I should throw all the lore out of the window? Forget it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that's what the Queen of England is doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>You</i> mentioned kings! And if Unconquered Sun weren't addicted to the Games he would be a perfect lord of Creation, as he showed during and after the Primordial War, up until he gave the Mandate to the Exalted, which in and of itself was still a great move, if inevitably short-sighted. The fact that Elizabeth II is just a glorified figurehead doesn't mean that a heroic queen/king wouldn't care for their subjects and lands, promote justice and welfare, and protect their kingdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, he fits at least one of the definitions of &quot;tyrant&quot; precisely.<br /> <br /> (&quot;A ruler who seized power without legal right.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ambiguity. Logical fallacy. While I greatly appreciate morally ambiguous characters, it doesn't net you any point in this argument. <i>Sol is not a tyrant, and we both know what I mean</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every management position requires delegating. Also, I don't care for that 2e-ism of the Sun having someone tend to his prayers, since that seems to indicate that people are praying to the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I don't care for a lot of things you're presenting as true. You want to stop arguing with me, or do you insist on trying to win the internets?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115406#post1115406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The river-god is not the river, why should the sun-god have to be?<br /> <br /> (Hell, among Celestial gods, the Ocean Father is viewed as something of a weirdo for spending so much of his time in Creation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Driving the Daystar is Unconquered Sun's duty as a god. Using it to repel armies of Raksha from Creation is Unconquered Sun's duty as a god. Using it to defend Creation from all outside threats is Unconquered Sun's duty as a god.<br /> <br /> And he's wasting time with the Games.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to reply to this, by all means. But I'm tiring of the discussion. So let me get back to your original grievances with my reply to Jen:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13651_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13651\" data-vbnamecard=\"13651\">Roswynn</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Actually, Solars have always been Anathema in Immaculate doctrine; since they never </span></span></span><i>fully</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> disappeared (only </span></span></span><i>mostly</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">), the Immaculates have been demonizing them as well as the Lunars.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not that it takes a thousand years of Immaculate doctrine for people to be afraid of Solars. The power they wield is scary, especially considering how messed-up humans can be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As for Abyssals, I wouldn't phrase it like that, namely because I doubt particular Abyssals want to destroy Creation in this edition. Are they resplendent with the powers of death and the Underworld? Yes. Does that make them &quot;hostile to Creation?&quot; Not notably more so than Solars, no.</span></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>Likewise on the notion of the Sun &quot;not doing his job.&quot; Answering prayers is not the job of the gods. In fact, it's generally a sign of dereliction of their duty</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit I was wrong on many accounts. Of course you're right, Solars have always been Anathema in Immaculate doctrine, since they never fully disappeared. And yes, I agree that people can be afraid of them, considering how powerful they are, and how human they are, and the Great Curse adds insult to injury. The fact that the Solar Exaltation <i>usually, from what Solars we've seen</i>, doesn't normally attach itself to complete monsters, and sometimes gets a perfectly decent human being, can contribute to them being seen as heroes <i>at least among some quarters</i>, like among the people who benefit from their acts, if any (I think the Icewalkers appreciate Yurgen Kaneko's rise as their war leader, even though their enhanced cohesion and aggressiveness will undoubtedly scare many neighbouring settlements, for good reason, as well as many decent people in the Realm, following the disastrous defeat of the powerful Tepet legions). &quot;A fortune of one means less for some&quot; (Sarah McLachlan, <i>World on Fire</i>) and in Creation, as in real life, the good guys don't always win, if they even really exist as something more than a sweeping generalization. So yeah, as Exalted keeps rightly asking us, &quot;</span></span></span><i>This is the world into which the Solar Exalted have returned \u2014 but will they save the world, or will they destroy it?</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, I was wrong there too. Destroying Creation doesn't seem, so far, a big priority. Hell, maybe it never was - I'm not knowledgeable enough in Exalted lore to be certain. Some Ex3 Abyssals simply do their thing, and even those who serve the Deathlords aren't hell-bent on destroying Creation, so far, as much as simply <i>serving the Deathlords</i>. Who can be downright nasty and even monstrously cruel, but aren't exactly trying a repeat of the Contagion, it would appear. Not that what we know so far depicts the Abyssals as particularly wholesome, but yes, my assertion that they simply want to destroy Creation is incorrect, I see it now. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Finally, Sol - yes, gods normally don't really answer prayers outside of some exceptions like Ahlat's hecatomb and <i>tauroboleum</i>, for instance (at least if what Ex2 told us is still at least partially valid; it appears that Alaht still can bless warriors even in Ex3, IIRC), but it certainly isn't their duty. So you're right again, that UCS doesn't answer his prayers is not ground enough to declare he's not doing his job. I still maintain that he has duties towards Creation and the Celestial Bureaucracy, and he's not attending to them, because Games of Divinity. You're free to disagree, but so far you've not convinced me my interpretation is wrong, at least on this count. I mean, someone might, I'm not made of stone. It's just that until now my impression hasn't been successfully challenged for me to change my mind. IMVHO Sol isn't doing his job. Free to disagree, agree to disagree, all that jazz.<br /> <br /> I'm done for now. Again, refute my previous points if you want. Not sure I'll get back to you on them. But hey, maybe you'll prove me wrong again - I don't hold any greater truth about the Exalted universe, I only read some stuff in some (2nd edition) PDFs and thought Jen might want to hear it.<br /> <br /> There. Back at ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:55:00-07:00","id":1115510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115403#post1115403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He seems to choose all of the Solars in Castebook though, there is even one Dawn slave on the Blessed Isle who keeps getting dreams of freedom from the Sun which is kinda hard to happen if he don't care who get exalted as his chosen.<br /> <br /> And I think that Ex3 follow this mode rather than the &quot;Automatic flying shard&quot; in Ex2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Really? But wait, when you talk about Castebook, you're referring to the 5 1st edition Caste Books, one for each flavour of Solar Exalted, which introduced new Charms and characters? Or is it something else I don't know about?<br /> <br /> I don't know if Ex3 follows the model you're referencing, Jen, in all honesty - I'm noticing I know less about Ex3 than I thought. If Unconquered Sun is actually <i>choosing</i> his Exalted, though, well, crap, that changes everything. He's not being an absentee deity anymore, not completely at least, and the Solars will definitely be very well-disposed towards him, I suppose, along with everyone the Solars help (while gaining the hatred of everyone the Solars hinder or degrade - but if he's choosing them, perhaps most Solars will actually be virtuous... not that they won't make enemies).<br /> <br /> If this were still Ex2 I would tell you the only difference is that now someone in Creation might actually be doing his will. He doesn't need anyone's prayers, he already receives all he needs from the Celestial Bureaucracy. So he doesn't need for the Solars to worship him, although that <i>might</i> please him. He doesn't <i>need</i> anyone to worship him. And he's still entangled in those freakin' Games, so that's what he cares most about (at least partly. He's probably intelligent enough to multitask, being the god of perfection and all that jazz).<br /> <br /> From what I've read of Ex3 (almost everything) and from what I remember, he doesn't appear to all Solars, just the Zeniths, as in Ex2, but at this point I'm open to any potential new revelation. I think it'd be way cooler if he actually <i>chose</i> his people, this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:56:44-07:00","id":1115511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115403#post1115403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think that Ex3 follow this mode rather than the &quot;Automatic flying shard&quot; in Ex2.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC the &quot;automatic flying shard&quot; is a safety feature. The primordials could have just ordered the incarne to stop exalting people, so they deliberately made sure that they physically couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:05:38-07:00","id":1115513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115511#post1115511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the &quot;automatic flying shard&quot; is a safety feature. The primordials could have just ordered the incarne to stop exalting people, so they deliberately made sure that they physically couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Niiice! Please someone tell me if you remember what page it is said UCS is actually choosing Solars this time around, I'd love if it were true!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T08:27:20-07:00","id":1115537,"title":"","content":"Spoilered for the sake of others.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new here, if you hadn't noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the forums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not well-versed in what direction the devs will take any aspect of Creation in the books. It would be slightly disingenuous to assume anyone knows what Holden, Morke, Vance or Minton have teased in posts on a forum, or that a preview PDF even exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't my intention to assume any knowledge on anyone's part. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, if you'd point me to this preview PDF i'd be grateful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a link handy - it was a Kickstarter backer reward, and while I backed the KS <i>after a fashion</i>, the rewards I got were secondhand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was <i>2003</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were the one to specify sixteen years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll let you ponder that).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's kind of a weird thing to bring up out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exploiting the dead like this and in the process obliterating them forever doesn't seem all that cute.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Deathlords are cute&quot; continues to not be my argument. Also, is it appreciably worse than dousing people in molten rubber to use as torches?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paints a pretty picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still hardly a world-ender. Calling the Abyssals and Deathlords a threat to life and the continued existence of Creation is like saying the same of Donald Trump - it's like, yeah, I see your point, but it's still something of an exaggeration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because at the time, the natural order of Creation had the Primordials at the top, the gods as their slaves, and humanity placed even lower than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what, the Unconquered Sun would philosophically watch as Creation burns, because everything must eventually die?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that if we're going into &quot;What if?&quot; territory, then even the Sun's intervention might not have saved the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>You</i> mentioned kings!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and in this case, his role as king of heaven seems largely ceremonial. He may have been made for the job, but he is not Creation's protector.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if Unconquered Sun weren't addicted to the Games he would be a perfect lord of Creation\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's agree to disagree on that one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Elizabeth II is just a glorified figurehead doesn't mean that a heroic queen/king wouldn't care for their subjects and lands, promote justice and welfare, and protect their kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming he wants to, sure, but whether it's because his hands are tied from the Mandate, or he's entranced by the Games, or just that seeing what his Chosen did in his name drove him to despair, he sure doesn't seem to want to do those things for Creation right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115502#post1115502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to stop arguing with me, or do you insist on trying to win the internets?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll stop here.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-13-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T09:03:01-07:00","id":1115549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115455#post1115455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading it just the other day, for the umpteenth time, believe it or not. Of course people tend to conflate weird supernatural beings with the word &quot;god&quot;. <i>A god</i>, not <i>the One True God</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand where you're getting this notion that a One True God is some distinct and provably false thing such that any number of them couldn't claim that thing. If you're arguing that most of the time they won't claim that they are literally the only spiritual being of power in the world, then sure! But if your intention is to say that people possess the means to parse the statement &quot;I am the only true god&quot; as verifiably false in Creation, that's no more true than saying they can verify that the Immaculate Philosophy isn't true.<br /> <br /> But perhaps since I'm being misunderstood. It is almost certainly a common thing for many beings to claim that they are a god and to claim that they are the only thing worthy of worship. The Censors of Heaven are corrupt or inept and the Gods do as they will. Elementals roam the earth and are regularly mistaken for gods. Ghosts appear to their ancestors and claim divinity and their worship. Exalts are worshipped as living gods (the Lunars fairly commonly!) and so on, but the notion that the people of Creation can look at any one of these things and say &quot;you aren't the One True God!&quot; as if the one true god is a single concept is absurd.<br /> <br /> And while we've been talking about gods doing it, we've also been ignoring cultures that may have simply invented their own deity within their cultures as well, which also happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115455#post1115455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't suppose to know what I've read and what I haven't, please, thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. A lot of people here discussing Exalted Third Edition have made some very confident and very peculiar claims about the knowledge that people possess in the setting, and your statements gave me the impression you were doing the same thing.<br /> <br /> People can't sort jack from jill, nevermind a one true god from a faker, and a lack of institutional knowledge in the average person means its fully possible for them to be told by any one entity that they are the only true wellspring of authority and power in the world, and they don't actually have the means to gainsay that. Seeing a Wood Spider trickster in the woods or an Honored Ancestor or even a City Father in the world does not actually mean that they have the capacity to gainsay that statement.<br /> <br /> More importantly, correcting the misunderstanding of the divine by mortals is not likely to show up as even a blip on the radar of the Celestial Bureaucracy. They would be far more theoretically concerned by the worship being accorded to those gods when they shouldn't be interfering with mortals at all, and as the setting demonstrates in examples from Great Forks to the Syndics to Ahlat, they're not really good at enforcing that separation anyway. The idea that they would be affronted or care at all that some tribe or city-state only believes in a single deity or ghost or elemental or Exalt or whatever is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Now, a next door neighbor deity who is angry about it and uses his connections to put resources in the Celestial Bureaucracy or allies of his own against those people? That's another question entirely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T09:20:19-07:00","id":1115552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115513#post1115513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Niiice! Please someone tell me if you remember what page it is said UCS is actually choosing Solars this time around, I'd love if it were true!!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if the book felt the need to be explicit about it, but <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">this wiki</a> is a repository of stated intentions for now and the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:16:08-07:00","id":1115574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115511#post1115511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the &quot;automatic flying shard&quot; is a safety feature. The primordials could have just ordered the incarne to stop exalting people, so they deliberately made sure that they physically couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kinda silly when you think about it - the Geas didn't make the gods have to do what the Primordials told them to; it just stopped them from harming them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:54:47-07:00","id":1115596,"title":"","content":"There were probably a few other measures in place though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:57:42-07:00","id":1115599,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Thank you for your welcome.<br /> <br /> Dousing people in molten rubber to use as torches? Who does that? What am I missing?<br /> <br /> Re: the above and rape, there was a place in the Underworld in 2nd Edition where the ghosts of serial rapists were moiled (is that the word? Moliated? Whatever) into beautiful women (of course) that could be raped scot-free for eternity. If my PC ever sees the place she's gonna burn it to the ground. So yeah, ghosts being forged into soulsteel is not the worst fate I can think of. As for why I specified the Loveless probably rape people, I wanted you to take notice of how monstrous a Deathlord can be... and some Abyssals serve them. Holy crap.<br /> <br /> It's just that Creation has a lot of problematic stuff going on... it sorta bothers me. That's all.<br /> <br /> At least we agree on Donald Trump. And yeah, I see now that the Abyssals aren't necessarily <i>all</i> laboring towards the final end of Creation. But the Deathlords, they started the Contagion. Crap, that almost ended Creation right there and then.<br /> <br /> So you think Unconquered Sun has his hands tied because of the Mandate? Or he's despairing because of what he saw his Chosen do in the 1st Age?... Uh. Interesting points.<br /> <br /> Yeah let's stop arguing. I don't like to argue. Also you sound like a clever person and I appreciate intelligence. Peace out for now.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:11:11-07:00","id":1115602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115510#post1115510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've read of Ex3 (almost everything) and from what I remember, he doesn't appear to all Solars, just the Zeniths, as in Ex2, but at this point I'm open to any potential new revelation. I think it'd be way cooler if he actually <i>chose</i> his people, this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I recall it was explained that he chooses unconsiously and couldn't stop himself even if he wanted to.<br /> It's kind of a middle ground where &quot;Chosen by the Unconquered Sun&quot; isn't purely symbolic, but you can still explore him as a cosmic deadbeat dad or the guy who made weapons to win a war and can't switch them off. I think for most PCs it simply doesn't matter if the Unconquered Sun doesn't fight their battles because he's selfish, bound by the Mandate, constrained by virtue, does too much collateral damage, doesn't want to hand out exaltations to every promising youth he sees or because he's higher than a kite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:21:37-07:00","id":1115608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115510#post1115510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if Ex3 follows the model you're referencing, Jen, in all honesty - I'm noticing I know less about Ex3 than I thought. If Unconquered Sun is actually <i>choosing</i> his Exalted, though, well, crap, that changes everything. He's not being an absentee deity anymore, not completely at least, and the Solars will definitely be very well-disposed towards him, I suppose, along with everyone the Solars help (while gaining the hatred of everyone the Solars hinder or degrade - but if he's choosing them, perhaps most Solars will actually be virtuous... not that they won't make enemies).</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 35. The degree to which the Unconquored Sun participates in the process is unconfirmed, but there's certainly no mention of <i>shards</i>. The second breath for Solars is <i>considered </i>to be the Unconquered Sun bestowing his blessing, though only the Zenith receive a visitation to proclaim this, for having somehow gained approval for deeds, accomplishments, potential, or expression. This does not require Solar Exalted to be, or remain, virtuous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:34:51-07:00","id":1115611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand where you're getting this notion that a One True God is some distinct and provably false thing such that any number of them couldn't claim that thing. If you're arguing that most of the time they won't claim that they are literally the only spiritual being of power in the world, then sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I'm doing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if your intention is to say that people possess the means to parse the statement &quot;I am the only true god&quot; as verifiably false in Creation, that's no more true than saying they can verify that the Immaculate Philosophy isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're not wrong. But since there's a lot of gods in Creation, and a lot of things people mistake for gods (ghosts, elementals, Exalted, demons, Raksha...), and they regularly show that they're at least as powerful as <i>that god over there</i>, it punches a hole in declaring &quot;I am the only true god&quot;. They'll wonder what's the difference. They'll probably be suspicious, I think. Of course an isolated culture who has contacts with a relatively powerful being and only relatively less powerful other beings will accept that the former is the one true god, sure. But people in Chiaroscuro, or Nexus, or, what's that city where they always have festivals for the gods... Great Forks! Well, those people should know better. There are lots of gods, some are your neighbors, others aren't really gods but you don't know, one comes up to you and says they're the only true god, you go &quot;Yeah, right&quot; and when you meet your priest you ask them. Not that the priest automatically has the straight dope, but they should have a modicum of knowledge about gods, considering their profession.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But perhaps since I'm being misunderstood. It is almost certainly a common thing for many beings to claim that they are a god and to claim that they are the only thing worthy of worship. The Censors of Heaven are corrupt or inept and the Gods do as they will. Elementals roam the earth and are regularly mistaken for gods. Ghosts appear to their ancestors and claim divinity and their worship. Exalts are worshipped as living gods (the Lunars fairly commonly!) and so on</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the notion that the people of Creation can look at any one of these things and say &quot;you aren't the One True God!&quot; as if the one true god is a single concept is absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they won't go to the being and tell them &quot;You're not the one true god&quot;, they'll just think there are many gods, because that's what they see, so when the being claims they are the only true god they will be like, &quot;What?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, like the Vikings (I actually mean Iron Age Scandinavians, not necessarily those who went raiding and trading with their longboats), when the Christian priests went and told them about God and Jesus, they nodded respectfully, and some appreciated the idea of the <i>Kvitekrist</i>, but they didn't abandon their whole pantheon just because the Christians said he was the One True God, the two faiths coexisted in sometimes confortable, sometimes rocky polytheism for centuries. A people who's used to lots and lots of gods thinks you're just another god, and can appreciate you, but they won't really grok the concept that all the other gods they've always known suddenly are just, whatever, angels, demons, spirits, djinn, Exalted, figments of their imaginations... right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies</div> </div> </div> </div>No need. Accepted. Don't worry at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people here discussing Exalted Third Edition have made some very confident and very peculiar claims about the knowledge that people possess in the setting, and your statements gave me the impression you were doing the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I have too made some very confident and peculiar claims about the knowledge that people possess in Creation, I've been essentially doing the same thing. And it's not like I know everything about the lore. So, guilty as charged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People can't sort jack from jill, nevermind a one true god from a faker, and a lack of institutional knowledge in the average person means its fully possible for them to be told by any one entity that they are the only true wellspring of authority and power in the world, and they don't actually have the means to gainsay that. Seeing a Wood Spider trickster in the woods or an Honored Ancestor or even a City Father in the world does not actually mean that they have the capacity to gainsay that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115549#post1115549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, correcting the misunderstanding of the divine by mortals is not likely to show up as even a blip on the radar of the Celestial Bureaucracy. They would be far more theoretically concerned by the worship being accorded to those gods when they shouldn't be interfering with mortals at all, and as the setting demonstrates in examples from Great Forks to the Syndics to Ahlat, they're not really good at enforcing that separation anyway. The idea that they would be affronted or care at all that some tribe or city-state only believes in a single deity or ghost or elemental or Exalt or whatever is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Now, a next door neighbor deity who is angry about it and uses his connections to put resources in the Celestial Bureaucracy or allies of his own against those people? That's another question entirely!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? If I tell you I'm the one true goddess and you stop worshipping the other gods in favor of just little ol' me, those gods will be angry because no prayers, no Essence, no peaches of immortality or whatever (I don't know how that works, I'm going by the seat of my pants) and will tell their superiors, and the Celestial Bureaucracy will know there's (another) problem. They already have a lot on their plate, they probably don't give a s**t, you're right, but sometimes, <i>sometimes</i>, they'll sic the Sids on the new one true goddess. Or find a way to manipulate some other Exalted into solving the problem for them. Or they have a look at me, see that my disruption is circumscribed to a small enough area, and get back to enjoying their peaches of immortality (yummy).<br /> <br /> But it's not just &quot;nothing&quot;. It's another problem among a multitude of probably more pressing matters, but not nothing.<br /> <br /> Anyways I think our positions are less distant than we thought. But, your turn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:58:14-07:00","id":1115618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115552#post1115552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if the book felt the need to be explicit about it, but <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">this wiki</a> is a repository of stated intentions for now and the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shiny! Thank you! I would prefer actual hard facts instead of stated intentions, and I'll more often use Ex2 with its complete lore instead of the tidbits we have to make do with for Ex3... and this is all Holden and Morke and other people who, AFAIK, no longer have a say in the project, right? Well, still, I'm sure it's an interesting read! Thanks again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:00:46-07:00","id":1115621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115611#post1115611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is it? If I tell you I'm the one true goddess and you stop worshipping the other gods in favor of just little ol' me, those gods will be angry because no prayers, no Essence, no peaches of immortality or whatever (I don't know how that works, I'm going by the seat of my pants) and will tell their superiors, and the Celestial Bureaucracy will know there's (another) problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't tell their superiors, because they are not supposed to be gaining worship from mortals in the first place. the One True Goddess and the other gods are both breaking the rules here, so there is no real appeal to authority where they don't both get in trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115611#post1115611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They already have a lot on their plate, they probably don't give a s**t, you're right, but sometimes, <i>sometimes</i>, they'll sic the Sids on the new one true goddess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but never solely because she claimed to be the one true goddess, it will be because of something else she did. If they were to hypothetically read off a list of offenses, &quot;claiming to be the only divinity&quot; would not even make it on the rolls, because there should be no claims of divinity and worship in the first place. To be clear, what I'm trying to convey is that when looking at a character like that, the notion of presenting themselves as a singular god or goddess and that being not true does not even register as a priority to correct, because that is not actually an affront to the divine order a priori. That individual gods might feel slighted is another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115611#post1115611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not just &quot;nothing&quot;. It's another problem among a multitude of probably more pressing matters, but not nothing.<br /> <br /> Anyways I think our positions are less distant than we thought. But, your turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to reiterate:<br /> <br /> Claiming to be the only god <i>is </i>nothing. It means nothing to the Celestial Bureaucracy or its laws, and it only means anything to other gods in a region, who may not do anything about it because they don't care or they lack the power, and the more powerful god acquiring the worship has better bribed Adiubande or Benadamaru or Wong Bongerok or Fakharu.<br /> <br /> However, <i>everything else </i>the theoretical one true goddess actually does is what might bring down the wrath of heaven. Interfering in mortal affairs or with Fate for instance. Killing people willy nilly, sure. Killing other gods, definitely. Trying to destroy them and weaken their purview, maybe (that probably happens a lot.) but that they claimed to be the only god is not an affront to Heaven. Heaven doesn't care what we believe, it cares about the practical consequences that such a god's actions might have for the world, their own interests and for Fate, and that condition occurs with or without making the claim to being a singular divinity.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to the fact that Heaven doesn't care what people believe, and this worship racketeering that goes on is not supposed to be happening anyway, which is why Gods manipulate mortals or Exalts or other beings into messing with one another. Incidentally its why we get to have fun stories where gods play people against one another and it isn't all an episode of Celestial Law &amp; Order.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm pushing back against the very specific assertions that people have the knowledge to confidently assert that something is wrong if they claim to be the only true divinity. They can see a million strange creatures and things in their lives. Some of those things will call themselves gods. Not all of them will be Gods. But a person in Creation literally does not have the intrinsic capability to distinguish one of these things from the other, and cannot confidently assert that it's a falsehood if one of them tells them they are the one true god. They might not believe them, but they are not in a position of power where they can say, with confidence that said creature is wrong. Which is probably why they run away and get a priest. Because a priest might say that. He may also lack the means to actually verify that this statement &quot;that I am the one true god and all these other things are false!&quot; but he will be better equipped to parley with strange things and will be able to handle the situation better.<br /> <br /> And the other specific assertion is that the Celestial Bureaucracy cares about this sort of thing. It'd be like if Prohibition Agents would come and arrest you a person drinking at an underground bar and they listed your crime as &quot;failure to correctly identify that the Rum was not Scotch.&quot; They may show up to arrest you, but it's because you're drinking! Not because you called the Rum a Scotch!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115618#post1115618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shiny! Thank you! I would prefer actual hard facts instead of stated intentions, and I'll more often use Ex2 with its complete lore instead of the tidbits we have to make do with for Ex3... and this is all Holden and Morke and other people who, AFAIK, no longer have a say in the project, right? Well, still, I'm sure it's an interesting read! Thanks again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth pointing out that Exalted Third Edition has been written to discard a vast majority of the assumptions that Second Edition brought to the game, and that you are definitely shooting yourself in the foot for discussion by using it as your reference point. You can ask the current developers in their thread if this still holds true, but a much better choice of reference would be Exalted's First Edition supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-13-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:26:14-07:00","id":1115629,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> <br /> <br /> Pleased to meet you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, he chooses unconsciously... middle grounds are so unfulfilling. I would've really liked for him to actually be <i>choosing</i> his Chosen, this time around.<br /> <br /> I agree that most PCs won't care for the actual reason Sol isn't on the battlefield with them, but I feel that if he spoke to all of them like he does with the Zeniths there would be more awe and cool in the setting. I have two prospective Dawns to run the game for, and a Twilight PC for later on, and none of them will ever hear UCS, much less see him, unless they actually go to Yu-Shan and manage to enter the JPD...<br /> <br /> Still... choosing unconsciously is still choosing, I guess. Perhaps it's already better than simply &quot;Automatic Flying Shard&quot; (which BTW folks, it should totally be the name of some lame-ass Charm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar487_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"487\" data-vbnamecard=\"487\">Greyman</a><br /> <br /> ... Weird. I've read that many times... I've never noticed the absence of the word &quot;shard&quot; in the description. On one hand it might not be there because it's a finer metaphysical point. But Lioness says UCS is actually choosing, albeit unconsciously, so there might be no shard at all. And you're right... in one sentence it's said that &quot;it's rare for cruel blackguards to gain the Unconquered Sun's blessing&quot;... and that many consider themselves righteous, although that doesn't stop them from going to war against each other... and then it says Solar Exaltation could bless anyone who deserves it, be they a saint or an assassin (well, no one wants Harmonious Jade to stop being a Solar). Well, I guess UCS in his wisdom sees the need for all kinds of people for the ranks of his Exalted.<br /> <br /> Okay, so he's choosing. No automatic flying shard. Mmm. I'll need to wrap my head around this. Perhaps the wiki Saur Ops Specialist linked might have something else of interest...<br /> <br /> ... Oh, and thank you! Both of you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:54:51-07:00","id":1115642,"title":"","content":"Last one and then I'm out of your hair.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115621#post1115621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They won't tell their superiors, because they are not supposed to be gaining worship from mortals in the first place. the One True Goddess and the other gods are both breaking the rules here, so there is no real appeal to authority where they don't both get in trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah... I see now... you're right. My position wasn't sufficiently well thought out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115621#post1115621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but never solely because she claimed to be the one true goddess, it will be because of something else she did. If they were to hypothetically read off a list of offenses, &quot;claiming to be the only divinity&quot; would not even make it on the rolls, because there should be no claims of divinity and worship in the first place. To be clear, what I'm trying to convey is that when looking at a character like that, the notion of presenting themselves as a singular god or goddess and that being not true does not even register as a priority to correct, because that is not actually an affront to the divine order a priori. That individual gods might feel slighted is another matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, now I understand. I agree, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115621#post1115621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to reiterate:<br /> <br /> Claiming to be the only god <i>is </i>nothing. It means nothing to the Celestial Bureaucracy or its laws, and it only means anything to other gods in a region, who may not do anything about it because they don't care or they lack the power, and the more powerful god acquiring the worship has better bribed Adiubande or Benadamaru or Wong Bongerok or Fakharu.<br /> <br /> However, <i>everything else </i>the theoretical one true goddess actually does is what might bring down the wrath of heaven. Interfering in mortal affairs or with Fate for instance. Killing people willy nilly, sure. Killing other gods, definitely. Trying to destroy them and weaken their purview, maybe (that probably happens a lot.) but that they claimed to be the only god is not an affront to Heaven. Heaven doesn't care what we believe, it cares about the practical consequences that such a god's actions might have for the world, their own interests and for Fate, and that condition occurs with or without making the claim to being a singular divinity.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to the fact that Heaven doesn't care what people believe, and this worship racketeering that goes on is not supposed to be happening anyway, which is why Gods manipulate mortals or Exalts or other beings into messing with one another. Incidentally its why we get to have fun stories where gods play people against one another and it isn't all an episode of Celestial Law &amp; Order.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm pushing back against the very specific assertions that people have the knowledge to confidently assert that something is wrong if they claim to be the only true divinity. They can see a million strange creatures and things in their lives. Some of those things will call themselves gods. Not all of them will be Gods. But a person in Creation literally does not have the intrinsic capability to distinguish one of these things from the other, and cannot confidently assert that it's a falsehood if one of them tells them they are the one true god. They might not believe them, but they are not in a position of power where they can say, with confidence that said creature is wrong. Which is probably why they run away and get a priest. Because a priest might say that. He may also lack the means to actually verify that this statement &quot;that I am the one true god and all these other things are false!&quot; but he will be better equipped to parley with strange things and will be able to handle the situation better.<br /> <br /> And the other specific assertion is that the Celestial Bureaucracy cares about this sort of thing. It'd be like if Prohibition Agents would come and arrest you a person drinking at an underground bar and they listed your crime as &quot;failure to correctly identify that the Rum was not Scotch.&quot; They may show up to arrest you, but it's because you're drinking! Not because you called the Rum a Scotch!</div> </div> </div> </div>Crystal clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115621#post1115621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth pointing out that Exalted Third Edition has been written to discard a vast majority of the assumptions that Second Edition brought to the game, and that you are definitely shooting yourself in the foot for discussion by using it as your reference point. You can ask the current developers in their thread if this still holds true, but a much better choice of reference would be Exalted's First Edition supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>am</i> shooting myself in the foot, ain't I? Ah, crap. I should simply steer clear from posts asking about the setting - and from posts asking about the mechanics too, since I'm not as good with them as other folks I've seen around. Or I could preface everything I say with &quot;Back in Ex2 when the world made sense to me... &quot;. Something like that. I might also try to learn what we know about Ex3... but Ex2 is so much more complete, whereas Ex3 right now is... sparse. Inchoate. Some interesting ideas (I love the Sea of Dreams and want it in my Creation too!... for instance), but few hard facts, even less juicy details... <i>sigh</i>. I just <i>can't</i> wait for all the official books to be published, at this rate I'll be an old woman when they're done...<br /> <br /> Heh, whatever. We'll see. Thanks for your patience (actually not just you, everyone in this thread, and poor Jen, who saw it being derailed by yours truly). As promised, I'm outta here.<br /> <br /> Ta-ta for now.<br /> <br /> Ros-</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:30:55-07:00","id":1115678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115618#post1115618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shiny! Thank you! I would prefer actual hard facts instead of stated intentions, and I'll more often use Ex2 with its complete lore instead of the tidbits we have to make do with for Ex3... and this is all Holden and Morke and other people who, AFAIK, no longer have a say in the project, right? Well, still, I'm sure it's an interesting read! Thanks again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The vision is highly likely to be maintained, seeing as how Vance and Minton, who are the two new developers, said a lot of what you can read there. There may be one other person aside from the prior developers who isn't there, but most of the people are still working on EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T16:26:04-07:00","id":1115711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115405#post1115405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you really think they'd do that? Why the hell would they care? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a corrupt system filled with racketeering AND they can according to the actual rules.<br /> <br /> Basically saying I am the supreme king shit is a challenge and people come at you for that (i here this is the premise of a number of biblical conflicts). Also likely there are still laws about fraud. Those laws exist to, effectivelly, prevent this. So the local mayor and capo don't do I rule your lives.<br /> <br /> If they are allowed to say it its because they are bribing someone high up enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T20:45:47-07:00","id":1115769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie#post1114985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religion, belief and worship in Exalted as presented in the book felt kinda weird to me, so if you guys don't mind me asking some question.......<br /> <br /> <b>1/</b> If a Solar is the roaming Creation freely type, then most of them will become less religious as they travel, aren't they ? Since meeting other spirits will makes them realize that their God is just merely a Terrestrial sky god and not some almighty creator who birth the world in seven day (this'll happen even early for Zenith).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Remember that Exalted religions usually don't teach that gods are omnipotent, omniscient flawless beings in the first place. While familiarity might breed contempt to an extent, and it's going to be natural for a Zenith to think differently about the gods when they realize they can punch them in the face, a god is still generally closely connected to some aspect of the world and to their worshippers, and it's not really unthinkable for a Zenith to develop more respect and sympathy for this <i>system</i>, when it works - for concept of divinity and the idea of gods working with humanity to achieve a better world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2/ </b>Is &quot;Cultural Christian&quot; a thing if you are a non-religious Solar, as in you celebrate a festival not because you believe in its backstory about a guy coming back from the dead, but more because it's your city's traditions/cultural identity and you aren't gonna stop eating those delicious cake just because the stories aren't real. Kinda like an atheist Jew who still attend Jewish holidays. </div> </div> </div>Some Solars might participate in their faith's trappings purely out of cultural affiliation rather than genuine religious devotion, sure - this would be especially true of they lost personal respect for a particular god, of course.<br /> <br /> But Confucianism (which is a big influence on Exalted, albeit more on the Sidereals and the Immaculate Faith than the Solars) tends to take the perspective that religion brings social benefits regardless of whether it is <i>true</i> or not. I could see many Exalted taking the same perspective (the Sidereals certainly do, and many DBs probably do as well) - even if you know that an individual god is corrupt, you might feel that there's value in retaining the traditions and structures around them, which can provide stability even if the god is personally weak or unworthy.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Exalted might also decide to solve the problem by punching the god's face off and replacing them with someone more worthy. They wouldn't necessarily see this as irreverent, if their devotion is to the system and its trappings rather than to an individual deity. On the other hand, punching a god's face off too often tends to lead to instability, which leads to internal conflicts as Exalted weigh these options against each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>3/ </b>Just in my house alone are the altar for my deceased grandparent, near it is the altar for the Buddhism pantheon, scattering around the house are altars to god of kitchen, the ground, luck, wealth, longevity...etc. In the street are temples and shrines to river gods, wandering ghosts, deified people or even animal like tiger.<br /> <br /> Is this suppose to be what most the religion landscape in Creation looks like i.e People follow a mixture of different beliefs and deities from various religions ? Since I heard that Creation is suppose to be animism and Shintoism or something, does that means place like Haborhead and Whitewall are oddballs since they only worship one supreme deity ? </div> </div> </div>Creation is huge! So there's a wide variety of stuff.<br /> <br /> In places that see less travel and where culture is more monolithic, I would expect to see more dedicated reverence for a single deity or a discrete clearly-defined group of deities (or a philosophy in some places, although the fact that the gods are real and have genuine power makes it hard for that to make serious inroads without supernatural backing, like the Immaculate Faith has). In these places the importance of an individual deity or group of deities could be exaggerated, sometimes even to the point of making them chief deity and treating them like the ruler of heaven.<br /> <br /> In areas with more cross-cultural contact, the kind of religious syncretism you described would be more common as different gods and faiths combine and form a common ground. But I suspect that while Creation has a lot of religious diversity, in most parts of the world it is <i>somewhat</i> constrained by the way certain religious facts are, well, <i>true</i> - there may be a few areas where an individually powerful god managed to establish monotheism (often dismissing or explaining lesser deities as eg. subservient spirits or angels or demons the way Christianity adapted many older deities into those roles), but that would be very rare. So a general understanding of &quot;there are a bunch of gods, as well as our ancestors, plus some distant celestial gods who rule over them&quot; is extremely common, with the main differences being over the exact Celestial Order, the attention and weight given to individual gods (with local ones often being exaggerated in importance), and the balance of attention paid to ancestors vs. gods - there would be <i>some</i> places that entirely deny parts or all of the basic understanding of Exalted's spiritual landscape, but they'd be isolated exceptions rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> (The Immaculate Faith is in some respects the big exception, of course, but even it doesn't really deny most of the basic aspects of the setting beyond putting the Elemental Dragons over the Incarnae and positing a different way in which people <i>ought</i> to interact with the divine. And it's able to be a big exception because it has a lot of influence and supernatural firepower behind it. Also, in the First Age and in areas where the Immaculate Faith has little sway, the hero cults of the Exalted themselves would sometimes form a bit of a third focus for worship alongside gods and ancestors.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-13-2017, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T20:55:33-07:00","id":1115771,"title":"","content":"Hmm, conversation seems to have resolved mostly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115537#post1115537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is it appreciably worse than dousing people in molten rubber to use as torches?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHeh, this touches on a subject that has been rolling around in my head for a while now, and that I might start a thread for. I just keep wondering whether the points I would bring up would be in good taste.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the moment, I personally kind of think that at least some of the Deathlords should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:19:44-07:00","id":1115780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13651_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13651\" data-vbnamecard=\"13651\">Roswynn</a> - I think one of the devs mentioned that they liken the Sun Choosing people as being akin to falling in love. Like, you can't really CONTROL that. Your eyes meet some stranger from across the room, there's a jolt, your heart speeds up, time seems to slow down... A Cracked.com video actually had one of the columnists note that &quot;Falling in love is the easy part. People do it all the time, by accident. With terrible people.&quot;<br /> <br /> It just so happens that when the Sun does this, the other person ends up glowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:43:39-07:00","id":1115789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115780#post1115780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the devs mentioned that they liken the Sun Choosing people as being akin to falling in love. Like, you can't really CONTROL that. Your eyes meet some stranger from across the room, there's a jolt, your heart speeds up, time seems to slow down... A Cracked.com video actually had one of the columnists note that &quot;Falling in love is the easy part. People do it all the time, by accident. With terrible people.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Swaim got some of that from his restraining order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:47:06-07:00","id":1115811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115769#post1115769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily. Remember that Exalted religions usually don't teach that gods are omnipotent, omniscient flawless beings in the first place. While familiarity might breed contempt to an extent, and it's going to be natural for a Zenith to think differently about the gods when they realize they can punch them in the face, a god is still generally closely connected to some aspect of the world and to their worshippers, and it's not really unthinkable for a Zenith to develop more respect and sympathy for this <i>system</i>, when it works - for concept of divinity and the idea of gods working with humanity to achieve a better world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a good example here is how many a head of state, including Kings and Emperors afforded absolute divine right and thought to be even more divine than Solars themselves... have often grown enamored of philosophers, mystics and prophets whom they have tried to emulate and follow the precepts of. This still happens in the modern day with many a guru whom the powerful follow.<br /> <br /> In fact, in said Gurus, the powerful often meet - you see many a head of state or powerful politician who meet under the auspices of gurus or weird churches whom they outrank and could destroy, in the real world.<br /> <br /> That says how easily it would be for Solars to worship Ahlat, and to meet in the worship of Ahlat and strike friendships based on their faith. The fact they could bring down his cult is no different than emperors being able to rout a cult with a word, and still deciding to follow all of its taboos. All it takes is the acceptance that to follow the precepts of that god leads to a healthier, more spiritually fulfilling life.<br /> <br /> ... and really, while Chosen sometimes have more raw power, it is important to note that chosen do not have the same kinds of powers, and are not the same kinds of entities. When you pray for a god, he can give you a blessing. Chosen normally cannot do it to each-other. If you are a devotee of Smiling Lover and believes she will give you luck in love... you know, that is something she can do. And blessings are invisible enough that you never know whether your luck in love comes from just following the precepts of her church, or from her actual blessings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 07-14-2017, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T03:03:18-07:00","id":1115858,"title":"","content":"I think people lean a bit too much into the falling in love analogy.<br /> <br /> \u200bAfter all, it's hardly the only thing that people do almost autonomously.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou'd have an easier time counting the things that are closer to being conscious and deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:12:54-07:00","id":1115908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115858#post1115858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people lean a bit too much into the falling in love analogy.<br /> <br /> \u200bAfter all, it's hardly the only thing that people do almost autonomously.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou'd have an easier time counting the things that are closer to being conscious and deliberate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another analogy was that getting the Incarnae to stop Exalting people is like telling someone to stop breathing. They can slow it down, but can't consciously stop forever.<br /> <br /> Unless they're dead but then it's not a choice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:34:40-07:00","id":1115922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115908#post1115908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another analogy was that getting the Incarnae to stop Exalting people is like telling someone to stop breathing. They can slow it down, but can't consciously stop forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's <i>too</i> autonomous, and I dislike the implication that the personality is absent besides.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink of it this way; ask me to never post in this forum again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:22:18-07:00","id":1116013,"title":"","content":"Like the Sun, I, too, can't stop myself from falling in love with burly old me....I mean heroes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-15-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:57:54-07:00","id":1116024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1115678#post1115678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vision is highly likely to be maintained, seeing as how Vance and Minton, who are the two new developers, said a lot of what you can read there. There may be one other person aside from the prior developers who isn't there, but most of the people are still working on EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I asked them, and Vance says they won't change anything just for the sake of <i>changing it</i>. It appears most things will follow the previous devs' vision. I've been re-reading their posts at the link you suggested (I noticed I had been there already some years ago, while waiting for Ex3 to come out), and there's a lot of good stuff, really. So... I think I'm alright with it!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>, the &quot;falling in love analogy&quot; is incredibly beautiful. I like it even more than deliberately choosing. And it explains a lot of how this &quot;unconscious choosing&quot; works. Just beautiful!<br /> <br /> ... Even if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> doesn't think it's apt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:59:10-07:00","id":1116047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116024#post1116024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Even if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> doesn't think it's apt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Isator's a grumpy old man. One who often has great insights about the setting - do give his posts much credence! ... but also keep in mind that's he's a grumpy old man (at heart, anyway) nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 07-14-2017, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:46:04-07:00","id":1116068,"title":"","content":"I don't think it isn't apt, per se, just that the map shouldn't be mistaken for the territory.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I'd make a point about it having possible issues with romanticising, but hey, it's not as if nobody ever fell in love with somebody who wasn't very good for them. If any setting has elements ready to deconstruct the idea that love is <u>universally</u> edifying and redemptive (as opposed to sometimes being so), it's this one.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a lot of previous posts to go through, has anybody brought up the idea that being Chosen by the Sun doesn't necessarily create a sense of obligation to the Sun yet? So it doesn't need to mean there'll always be Solars who feel positively towards him, in a religious manner or otherwise?<br /> <br /> \u200bI've been thinking a lot lately about what it would mean in the First Age to have a Solar who could be regarded as evil, without undermining the idea of them being Chosen, creating a sense of Exaltation as something wholly immoral and indiscriminate, or stepping on the toes of the Great Curse. <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:21:07-07:00","id":1116082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116068#post1116068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it isn't apt, per se, just that the map shouldn't be mistaken for the territory.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I'd make a point about it having possible issues with romanticising, but hey, it's not as if nobody ever fell in love with somebody who wasn't very good for them. If any setting has elements ready to deconstruct the idea that love is <u>universally</u> edifying and redemptive (as opposed to sometimes being so), it's this one.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a lot of previous posts to go through, has anybody brought up the idea that being Chosen by the Sun doesn't necessarily create a sense of obligation to the Sun yet? So it doesn't need to mean there'll always be Solars who feel positively towards him, in a religious manner or otherwise?<br /> <br /> \u200bI've been thinking a lot lately about what it would mean in the First Age to have a Solar who could be regarded as evil, without undermining the idea of them being Chosen, creating a sense of Exaltation as something wholly immoral and indiscriminate, or stepping on the toes of the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd compare first age takes on solars to some social notions of sacredness. The Solar is sacred, powerful, full of mana. But that doesn't mean they are good or safe. If anything, they are extremely dangerous! Especially if unwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:01:43-07:00","id":1116121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116068#post1116068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHmm, I'd make a point about it having possible issues with romanticising, but hey, it's not as if nobody ever fell in love with somebody who wasn't very good for them. If any setting has elements ready to deconstruct the idea that love is <u>universally</u> edifying and redemptive (as opposed to sometimes being so), it's this one.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen someone respond to the falling in love analogy with &quot;I love this because <i>it means that our characters can turn out to be horrible and we can break the Sun's heart</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the point of the Love analogy was that it's something that happens, and not something the Sun can always control, save by, say, literally turning away from Creation. And even then it's not totally foolproof, as seen by the fact that there were SOME Solars between the Usurpation and whatever caused the Sun to face Creation again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T16:11:34-07:00","id":1116143,"title":"","content":"He's not saying it's a bad analogy - we just need to be careful not to confuse &quot;like&quot; for &quot;is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:34:37-07:00","id":1116377,"title":"","content":"On a tangent, I came across this description of the influence of the gods in the Iliad:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Julian Jaynes, The Origin of Consciousness in the Breakdown of the Bicameral Mind*, Chapter 3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Agamemnon, king of men, robs Achilles of his mistress, it is a god that grasps Achilles by his yellow hair and warns him not to strike Agamemnon (I :197ff.). It is a god who then rises out of the gray sea and consoles him in his tears of wrath on the beach by his black ships, a god who whispers low to Helen to sweep her heart with homesick longing, a god who hides Paris in a mist in front of the attacking Menelaus, a god who tells Glaucus to take bronze for gold (6:234ff.), a god who leads the armies into battle, who speaks to each soldier at the turning points, who debates and teaches Hector what he must do, who urges the soldiers on or defeats them by casting them in spells or drawing mists over their visual fields. It is the gods who start quarrels among men (4:437ff.) that really cause the war (3:164ff.), and then plan its strategy (2:56ff.). It is one god who makes Achilles promise not to go into battle, another who urges him to go, and another who then clothes him in a golden fire reaching up to heaven and screams through his throat across the bloodied trench at the Trojans, rousing in them ungovernable panic. In fact, the gods take the place of consciousness.<br /> <br /> The beginnings of action are not in conscious plans, reasons, and motives; they are in the actions and speeches of gods. To another, a man seems to be the cause of his own behavior. But not to the man himself. When, toward the end of the war, Achilles reminds Agamemnon of how he robbed him of his mistress, the king of men declares, &quot;Not I was the cause of this act, but Zeus, and my portion, and the Erinyes who walk in darkness: they it was in the assembly put wild ate upon me on that day when I arbitrarily took Achilles' prize from him, so what could I do? Gods always have their way.&quot; (19:86-90).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess that in the world of Creation, omnipresent religious experience are not part of the world in this way. The gods (including the Incarna!) don't speak directly into the minds of humanity, don't have an omnipresent influence. This doesn't seem to be part of the fiction, and various factors in the setting militate strongly against it, not least how social influence and integrity is construed, and the idea that the Mandate of Heaven is given to the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Instead human in Creation mostly influence each other, or act according to their own psychology. They are those kind of heroes.<br /> <br /> So curious what happens in people's games, with the Solars and other Exalted. Do your games emulate at all relationships like the above between human and god or is it much more hands off? Would it be fun to do Exalted, or a mythic fantasy roleplaying game, the way that the above excerpts work and with the gods having that kind of influence and presence?<br /> <br /> (Truncated from a longer reply. This thread kind of inspires a few of thoughts in me about the tension between polytheism and monotheism, between moral religion and amoral religion, how necessary divinity as the creator is to religion. But I couldn't go anywhere with them!).<br /> <br /> *You can ignore the text it's from, as the argument that makes, about the degree to which this literally represents a description of the ancient thought process, is not really so relevant to what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:37:33-07:00","id":1116490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116377#post1116377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would guess that in the world of Creation, omnipresent religious experience are not part of the world in this way. The gods (including the Incarna!) don't speak directly into the minds of humanity, don't have an omnipresent influence. This doesn't seem to be part of the fiction, and various factors in the setting militate strongly against it, not least how social influence and integrity is construed, and the idea that the Mandate of Heaven is given to the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Instead human in Creation mostly influence each other, or act according to their own psychology. They are those kind of heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's that, but there's also the question of things like the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething I've considered for a while is the subject of whether or not anything about gods might help people to form systems of insight into themselves or the world that might form a strong path to personal satisfaction, fulfilment, or general contentment. That even if most gods, as people, aren't very numinous, if there's anything deriving from their nature as gods that could help people devise useful paths of mysticism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:28:39-07:00","id":1116504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116490#post1116490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's that, but there's also the question of things like the Bureau of Destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;If you think we are not very influential, look at all the objects around you, just lying there. That's all us.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:57:13-07:00","id":1116519,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I feel as though Fate as the laws of physics should be played down a bit from herein. I don't think it was exactly a bad idea, but it doesn't quite matter to the driving motivations of actors in the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, the Bureau isn't divided into Departments of Falling Objects and Temperature, the constellations don't place governing the motion of bodies through space front and centre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:34:08-07:00","id":1116535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116519#post1116519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel as though Fate as the laws of physics should be played down a bit from herein. I don't think it was exactly a bad idea, but it doesn't quite matter to the driving motivations of actors in the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, the Bureau isn't divided into Departments of Falling Objects and Temperature, the constellations don't place governing the motion of bodies through space front and centre.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always took that line to be far more subtle than 'laws of physics'. You are in the world Fate makes, with each moment, as it arranges the chairs and players of Creation's grand drama.<br /> <br /> Making it something as crude, direct and unyielding as laws of physics was certainly a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:51:27-07:00","id":1116687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie#post1114985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr /><br /> Religion, belief and worship in Exalted as presented in the book felt kinda weird to me, so if you guys don't mind me asking some question.......<br /> <br /> <b>1/</b> If a Solar is the roaming Creation freely type, then most of them will become less religious as they travel, aren't they ? Since meeting other spirits will makes them realize that their God is just merely a Terrestrial sky god and not some almighty creator who birth the world in seven day (this'll happen even early for Zenith).<br /> <br /> <b>2/ </b>Is &quot;Cultural Christian&quot; a thing if you are a non-religious Solar, as in you celebrate a festival not because you believe in its backstory about a guy coming back from the dead, but more because it's your city's traditions/cultural identity and you aren't gonna stop eating those delicious cake just because the stories aren't real. Kinda like an atheist Jew who still attend Jewish holidays.<br /> <br /> <b>3/ </b>Just in my house alone are the altar for my deceased grandparent, near it is the altar for the Buddhism pantheon, scattering around the house are altars to god of kitchen, the ground, luck, wealth, longevity...etc. In the street are temples and shrines to river gods, wandering ghosts, deified people or even animal like tiger.<br /> <br /> Is this suppose to be what most the religion landscape in Creation looks like i.e People follow a mixture of different beliefs and deities from various religions ? Since I heard that Creation is suppose to be animism and Shintoism or something, does that means place like Haborhead and Whitewall are oddballs since they only worship one supreme deity ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my understanding:<br /> <br /> 1) Creation has no concept of an all-powerful sky god who birthed the world in seven days to lose faith in in the first place. Why would their beliefs change (in this manner, anyway)?<br /> <br /> 2) Keep in mind that gods are established facts in Creation as obvious and immutable as gravity, and that (iirc) you don't need to actually believe/trust in the god you're praying to in order for your prayer/devotion to give them power. Most of the gods require a particular ritual be performed in their honor, rather than that those who pray to them have actual faith.<br /> <br /> 3) It's more accurate to compare the gods to a local government (see the term Heavenly Bureaucracy). They're certainly powerful, but there are other gods elsewhere who manage similar tasks, and gods within their own area that outrank them. The god of This River in the South isn't also the god of That River in the North East, even if functionally speaking they're similar. There's little reason to pray to gods on the other side of the world when one nearby can do the same thing for you for the same effort (the obvious exception being extremely pious priests and the like who the gods will empower no matter where they are)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T02:22:33-07:00","id":1116767,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered, honestly, why so many Solars in the fluff seem to worship the UCS.<br /> <br /> I mean, most Solars have been exalted for 2-3 years. They don't have high ratings of Lore and Occult. Do they even know that the UCS granted them these powers? Do they even know who the UCS is? Even Zeniths, who get a message from him, aren't generally shown as getting a message where he explains who he is, it's just a mysterious voice.<br /> <br /> I'd expect most Solars to either worship the same local Gods they always did, the Gods of their culture, or be in a state of religious flux due to the massive change in their life.<br /> But it's not like becoming a Solar is followed 3 days later by a delivery of a book explaining how the UCS is God of Solars and you should totally worship him.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, the only Solar PCs I've seen in my games who worshipped the UCS were those who were taught by the Cult of the Illuminated. The rest either don't care much about the Gods, or worship the Gods of their people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:24:25-07:00","id":1116794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116519#post1116519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel as though Fate as the laws of physics should be played down a bit from herein. I don't think it was exactly a bad idea, but it doesn't quite matter to the driving motivations of actors in the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, the Bureau isn't divided into Departments of Falling Objects and Temperature, the constellations don't place governing the motion of bodies through space front and centre.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nerds worship science and engineering. Or more accurately the kind of reverence and devotion or even acceptance that we associate with the laws of physics science Technology and Engineering is something that would be much more akin to the kind of forces that you would have to fight in your own mind if you have a religious mindset. Even if that religious mindset is hypocritical second-guessed double conscious whenever you want to call it it's not something that you could completely turn off and ignore. So equating fate with physics was honestly a master stroke. Unfortunately you run into the other problem with nerd discourse. Basically if you got the most science or technical things then everything else is subservient to that. So effectively they said that the setting didn't work like they said it did and then made it the exclusive province of one group that was so damn good at it that no one else could stop them except for the fact that they had enslavement limiters on. And short they made a game so likely to a lot of prospective it guys and then they one faction at the it reality ninjas. Yeah that was always going to backfire <br /> But just like exalting is like Falling in Love fate is like physics is a very good working analogy and metaphor for understanding how the characters will live their lives interact with their setting and think about things. Especially when you have to tell physics to go screw a lot in order to just make the most simple charms work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:31:48-07:00","id":1116795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116767#post1116767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered, honestly, why so many Solars in the fluff seem to worship the UCS.<br /> <br /> I mean, most Solars have been exalted for 2-3 years. They don't have high ratings of Lore and Occult. Do they even know that the UCS granted them these powers? Do they even know who the UCS is? Even Zeniths, who get a message from him, aren't generally shown as getting a message where he explains who he is, it's just a mysterious voice.<br /> <br /> I'd expect most Solars to either worship the same local Gods they always did, the Gods of their culture, or be in a state of religious flux due to the massive change in their life.<br /> But it's not like becoming a Solar is followed 3 days later by a delivery of a book explaining how the UCS is God of Solars and you should totally worship him.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, the only Solar PCs I've seen in my games who worshipped the UCS were those who were taught by the Cult of the Illuminated. The rest either don't care much about the Gods, or worship the Gods of their people.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in previous Editions exaltation came with infusions of past lives. This was how you got super fast at certain skills you weren't learning them from scratch you were relearning them from your past self. Also while every zenith gets a visitation other cast may get a visitation or their exaltation maybe a highly personalized experience. As an example there was a Twilight cast that literally had a vision of one of his past selves talking to him and possibly even influencing him to help Servite itsy afterwards he spent weeks in a delirium at a house with his wife and two daughters. When can you merge do you have the basic understandings of sorcery and the ability to use his Magics to a more advanced level and learn how to gain access to more.<br /> all of these memories are filtered both through the recent Incarnation as well as apparently there's some editing going on up in heaven. But the idea is it supposed to give you a basic idea of what your past self was and what they experienced and because the exalted culture even and its decline was all about the power of the sun and the Sun is still up there even if not as understood or as communicative well chances are they're going to run into billions and billions of triggers each day that goes holy s*** I was a child or champion god-king who was exalted by right of the Sun god.<br /> this is why the cast books often have sections of recollections a past lives. These can get even stronger once they run into a lunar mate or something. Once they go dungeon diving for their old gear they're going to have even more memories pop up telling them what they experienced and why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:01:10-07:00","id":1116803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116795#post1116795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">all of these memories are filtered both through the recent Incarnation as well as apparently there's some editing going on up in heaven</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to point out, if by &quot;editing going up in Heaven&quot;, you're referring to Lytek, that was the case in Ex2, but he totally can't do anything of the sort in the current edition AFAIK - he no longer has <i>any</i> power over Exaltations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:40:16-07:00","id":1116811,"title":"","content":"Lytek hasn't been mentioned in the corebook, because he doesn't matter to it, but he's probably still going to be in the game, and have about the same role.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T06:12:03-07:00","id":1116822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116811#post1116811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lytek hasn't been mentioned in the corebook, because he doesn't matter to it, but he's probably still going to be in the game, and have about the same role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I messed up. I misremembered a quote by John Morke during <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the interregnum before Ex3 was published:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lytek does indeed still exist. He is a functionary within the Heavenly Bureaucracy. He doesn't have </span></span></span><u>any</u><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> say in who gets Chosen&quot;. (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/3E_Setting#Exalts_and_Exaltation\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/...and_Exaltation</a>, last answer before the &quot;Gods and Yu-Shan&quot; section)</span></span></span>. You're absolutely right of course, he hasn't been mentioned yet in this edition (so things might well change, too).<br /> <br /> Please disregard my previous comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T07:21:20-07:00","id":1116833,"title":"","content":"He never did have any say over who was Chosen. On the subject of worshipping Unconquered sun, basically everyone in Creation worships Him. He is the greatest of gods, King of Heaven. Of course people worship him. This is a polytheistic society, people worship, by definition, many gods. Even priests of other gods worship him, just as His priests give worship to other gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T07:39:58-07:00","id":1116836,"title":"","content":"....Very few people actually worship the UCS. He is a mostly forgotten god, either because he is presumed to be unconcerned with mortal affairs and too distant, or because he answers very few prayers.<br /> IIRC, only a few tribes near Harborhead actually praise him directly these days. While many mythologies might include Him, and the Maidens, very few veiw him as the most important object of worship, if only because he so rarely interacts with peoples lives. FErtillity? You'll get better results from the Field Gods. War? Check your direction, they'll be more intreasted. The Incarnae, UCS included, don't typically have reverance in creation outside of specific indviduals (Desert hermits and madmen, beastmen instructed by lunars, star-obsessed sages).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T08:19:28-07:00","id":1116841,"title":"","content":"He's also not the only sun god.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:00:11-07:00","id":1116853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116833#post1116833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of worshipping Unconquered sun, basically everyone in Creation worships Him. He is the greatest of gods, King of Heaven. Of course people worship him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do <i>they</i> know that? How does Joe Subsistence Farmer know who's in charge in a city he'll never see, an incalculable distance away? Who told him, why, and how did he come to the decision that he needs to devote any of his meager income to gratifying a spirit who is never going to do anything for him?<br /> <br /> Individuals may still worship him, but by and large the Sun's prayer allotment stems from the 10% tithe on all the prayer in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:26:01-07:00","id":1116861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116833#post1116833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a polytheistic society</div> </div> </div> </div>There are about twenty different societies in the core.<br /> <br /> Not all of them could really be called polytheistic.<br /> <br /> \u200b(To the extent that that's really an accurate description of any religious system anyway; it's my understanding that it's beginning to lose credibility)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:34:44-07:00","id":1116864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116853#post1116853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do <i>they</i> know that? How does Joe Subsistence Farmer know who's in charge in a city he'll never see, an incalculable distance away? Who told him, why, and how did he come to the decision that he needs to devote any of his meager income to gratifying a spirit who is never going to do anything for him?<br /> <br /> Individuals may still worship him, but by and large the Sun's prayer allotment stems from the 10% tithe on all the prayer in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's the god of a giant fire ball on the sky, such an eye-catching thing will attract attention one way or another I think.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder, what happen when you pray to the sun in general and not TUCS specifically, or if you pray to an imaginary sun god, or a god who pretend to be a sun deity ? Does your prayer create ambrosia, and where will it go ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:06:39-07:00","id":1116956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116841#post1116841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's also not the only sun god.</div> </div> </div> </div>What other sun gods are there, and where do I find them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:34:03-07:00","id":1116963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116956#post1116956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other sun gods are there, and where do I find them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're only mentioned in passing so we don't know much about them.<br /> Glories Luna page 14 mentions the god of Eclipses born of a union between The Unconquered Sun and Luna.<br /> Compass Yu-Shan page 44 mentions &quot;Thelmarin, Eastern Goddess of Peace and Twilight&quot;<br /> <br /> Not a sun god, but also in Yu-Shan is Sano-Medaro a Lesser Elemental Dragon in the Bureau of Nature with the title &quot;Daimyo of Sunshine&quot; a position which probably also takes its cut of prayer directed to the sun as celestial object associated with good weather. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:44:12-07:00","id":1116965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116963#post1116963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're only mentioned in passing so we don't know much about them.<br /> Glories Luna page 14 mentions the god of Eclipses born of a union between The Unconquered Sun and Luna.<br /> Compass Yu-Shan page 44 mentions &quot;Thelmarin, Eastern Goddess of Peace and Twilight&quot;<br /> <br /> Not a sun god, but also in Yu-Shan is Sano-Medaro a Lesser Elemental Dragon in the Bureau of Nature with the title &quot;Daimyo of Sunshine&quot; a position which probably also takes its cut of prayer directed to the sun as celestial object associated with good weather.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I get it - they're gods related to specific aspects of the sun, right? Not, like, real rivals to UCS, in the sense that they also are linked to the Sun itself. That's only UCS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T14:25:40-07:00","id":1116978,"title":"","content":"I like to grant even non Zeniths a little bit of a visitation so they feel more connection to the sun. But I think the more default answer is &quot;your circle's zenith convinces you to worship the UCS.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I thought it was normal for the UCS to be understood, just thought of as distant and unconcerned with you, but I'm AFB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:41:19-07:00","id":1117021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116864#post1116864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's the god of a giant fire ball on the sky, such an eye-catching thing will attract attention one way or another I think.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder, what happen when you pray to the sun in general and not TUCS specifically, or if you pray to an imaginary sun god, or a god who pretend to be a sun deity ? Does your prayer create ambrosia, and where will it go ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Day and Night and the ball in the sky are.. I mean even if not distinct entities of themselves are associated with entities. I mean they kind of have to be. The Sun is.. like the most obvious influence on the world. Plants and blind people know about it.<br /> <br /> I am agreeing with you. And considering it has a person who they all owe their paychecks AND lives to you would think they wouldn't freely I don't know short him.<br /> <br /> How many people have met the Scarlet Empress, heck possibly Dragonblooded have gone their lives without an appearance. Aside from in the inside some of her children are virtual strangers.<br /> <br /> But everyone respects and knows who she is. And if not that can be rectified.<br /> <br /> I imagine its like with gods and spirits and the Sun. While not addressed by his full sobriquet or personal name or culture given name the effects and actions got to be there. Also Kejak was noted to have included the Incarna on the prayer schedule as needed.<br /> <br /> Still part of not gaining his attention in heaven is making sure things run smooth enough without him without him feeling muscled out. So wahtever is important to his office for him needs to still be there. Admittedly depends, as intended, just HOW addicted and absentee you want him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116978#post1116978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to grant even non Zeniths a little bit of a visitation so they feel more connection to the sun. But I think the more default answer is &quot;your circle's zenith convinces you to worship the UCS.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I thought it was normal for the UCS to be understood, just thought of as distant and unconcerned with you, but I'm AFB.</div> </div> </div> </div>PRetty much that's the doctrine of the Immaculates. The pagan/hundred gods heresy might say anything at any place and time but do recall this guy fought a war to free them AND evidence of his existence marks the flows of time. so uhm.. ya know even if they don't worship him or tell their followers you have to figure they speak with some respect of his rule or authority like sailors, even deeply dissolute nonbelievers, do of Neptune or The Sea as an entity as to a phenomenon<br /> or some do Right or Law","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 07-16-2017, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:20:51-07:00","id":1117104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116965#post1116965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I get it - they're gods related to specific aspects of the sun, right? Not, like, real rivals to UCS, in the sense that they also are linked to the Sun itself. That's only UCS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The lesser solar deities are probably going to be irrelevant to most Exalted games but their existence does help to explain why worship of The Unconquered Sun has faded to the extent it has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:01:45-07:00","id":1117286,"title":"","content":"I think there are religious systems and mythological cycles in which, while the sun might be acknowledged, it's not very prominent. It's possible for people to form belief systems in which it's just another feature of the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven without the historical context of this setting that would push people away from explicit worship of the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:24:55-07:00","id":1117304,"title":"","content":"Now I'm thinking about some of the circumstances surrounding changing levels of esteem for gods in a few societies, such as Roman and Egyptian.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven in cases where one of the Exalted doesn't take their personal relationship with the Unconquered Sun as a reason for worship, there are advantages to championing an obscure deity. It can provide a framework by which one establishes themselves as a new political bloc, invoking the legitimacy of something distantly familiar while also using the way it is uncommon as a means of distinguishing yourself, allowing your achievements to stand out more and garner more popularity. It also gives you the advantage of appealing to people disillusioned with the status quo by selling them on something with the advantage of novelty. Alternatively, it can serve as a means by which one projects their own rise to power, becoming the language through which your ascendency is stated and discussed. That one isn't even necessarily about making people worship the god, so much as making monuments to it the visible symbol of your presence in their lives<br /> <br /> \u200bThose are the kinds of things that happened when the adherents of Cybele (a deity of Phrygian origin) in the Roman Senate held her up as a key to Rome's salvation during the Second Punic War, or how Amun rose from being the god of the relatively minor city of Thebes to being conflated with the sun god Ra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:34:38-07:00","id":1117804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1117286#post1117286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are religious systems and mythological cycles in which, while the sun might be acknowledged, it's not very prominent. It's possible for people to form belief systems in which it's just another feature of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. But if there's no sun worship without it being spurned on by someone who knows about the Unconquered Sun like the Sidereals or the Dragon Kings it\u2019s in danger of becoming conspicuous in its absence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:29:34-07:00","id":1117906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116767#post1116767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered, honestly, why so many Solars in the fluff seem to worship the UCS.<br /> <br /> I mean, most Solars have been exalted for 2-3 years. They don't have high ratings of Lore and Occult. Do they even know that the UCS granted them these powers? Do they even know who the UCS is? Even Zeniths, who get a message from him, aren't generally shown as getting a message where he explains who he is, it's just a mysterious voice.<br /> <br /> I'd expect most Solars to either worship the same local Gods they always did, the Gods of their culture, or be in a state of religious flux due to the massive change in their life.<br /> But it's not like becoming a Solar is followed 3 days later by a delivery of a book explaining how the UCS is God of Solars and you should totally worship him.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, the only Solar PCs I've seen in my games who worshipped the UCS were those who were taught by the Cult of the Illuminated. The rest either don't care much about the Gods, or worship the Gods of their people.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of my Solars worship the UCS for precisely this reason.<br /> <br /> Varied Paths: I noticed after assigning her mechanical stats that all of her merits were physical in nature (giantism, pain tolerance, etc etc) so I fluffed it that they came BEFORE she Exalted. So she worships Zelos, a god of strength who is responsible for most of her pre-exalted prowess. This might change in the future if she meets UC(ena)S, but I doubt it. She would not take the knowledge that he essentially abandoned the world to its fate well, especially given how badly the Realm is screwing everything up.<br /> <br /> Not-Saber: This one I don't remember the name of, but you can guess what she was like from the name. She did follow the sort of ideals UCS wanted his Chosen to follow (leadership, helping others, bravery, etc etc) but she had no opinion on the god himself. (I've since reworked her as Varied Paths' first age incarnation - there she very much worshipped the sun, but that's the first age, so not really an issue).<br /> <br /> Silent Mask: This guy was an assassin for hire that was only loyal to his Khan and to the Tri-Khan. 'Nuff said. But he was in a game where one of the other PCs was from a secretive cult that worshipped the Sun and guarded a gate to the Underworld from which a demon rampaged out one day. (I was new to Exalted at the time so I didn't realize how confusing this was and didn't really question it)<br /> <br /> Boisterous Fire of the Welcoming Hearth: This guy's game never really got off the ground, but he was a Zenith, so he probably would've heard something from Sol. I never really decided what that was, but given that one of his goals was also to build a giant harem for the sake of political manipulation and manuevering, I doubt he and Sol would have gotten along. (On the other hand, Hearth also genuinely wanted to help people who had been hurt or traumatized by their lives, so... make of that what you will)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:36:30-07:00","id":1117962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116767#post1116767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered, honestly, why so many Solars in the fluff seem to worship the UCS.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got a point there. Hm, I'll bandwagon...<br /> <br /> My Dawn, Aaliyah... Well she doesn't WORSHIP many Gods... But that comes from her having been the daughter of an Elemental Dragon. She knew smaller Gods and Spirits, speaks Old Realm, but doesn't WORSHIP many of them. That said, when I said &quot;I can imagine many Solars making offerings, but mostly to be polite&quot; I was mostly thinking of her.<br /> <br /> My Twilight, Amilar Harken, still considers himself... Eh, an <i>alright</i> Immaculate in that he tries to better himself and the world. And he still swears using the names of the Dragons, because some things are ingrained.<br /> <br /> Now my Zenith, Yi Ling, DOES revere the Sun... But he appeared before her and Chose her, speaking to her. She eventually goes on a long pilgrimage to try and find out WHY she, a bitter and angry former Dynast who ran away from home, was Chosen by the Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T01:25:52-07:00","id":1118109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1117104#post1117104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The lesser solar deities are probably going to be irrelevant to most Exalted games but their existence does help to explain why worship of The Unconquered Sun has faded to the extent it has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Kind of like how Apollo largely displaced Helios in Greek mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T02:00:18-07:00","id":1118452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116965#post1116965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I get it - they're gods related to specific aspects of the sun, right? Not, like, real rivals to UCS, in the sense that they also are linked to the Sun itself. That's only UCS.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other gods with different domains might also be worshiped as sun gods. At my own table, I ruled in these cases they just pay an extra tax out of their ambrosia to the Unconquered Sun. Ahlat is worshiped as a sun-god in Harborhead, Golden-Eyed Jorst by the Linnowans (fitting his cyclical rising and declining and rising again themes), the Golden Lord by An-Teng, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T08:24:47-07:00","id":1118970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116836#post1116836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Very few people actually worship the UCS. He is a mostly forgotten god, either because he is presumed to be unconcerned with mortal affairs and too distant, or because he answers very few prayers.<br /> IIRC, only a few tribes near Harborhead actually praise him directly these days. While many mythologies might include Him, and the Maidens, very few veiw him as the most important object of worship, if only because he so rarely interacts with peoples lives. FErtillity? You'll get better results from the Field Gods. War? Check your direction, they'll be more intreasted. The Incarnae, UCS included, don't typically have reverance in creation outside of specific indviduals (Desert hermits and madmen, beastmen instructed by lunars, star-obsessed sages).</div> </div> </div> </div>The UCS is one of the most widely worshiped Gods in Creation. The Immaculate Order worships him as a primary deity, confusing as that is.<br /> <br /> Most Solar Exalted who are exposed to the 'church of the UCS' are going to come into contact with the corrupted Immaculate interpretation first. Obviously, given the unique flavor of this interpretation, they may reject the notion that they have 'stolen' power from anything (particularly if they are Zenith).<br /> <br /> However, if one can somehow manage to discard the stuff about calling up demons to steal celestial energy, the UCS in the Immaculate Faith is more or less the same God that was worshiped in the mother culture prior to the Contagion and prior to the Shogunate. It's very likely that key details and aspects of that faith which survive are more or less accurate.<br /> <br /> The worship of the UCS might seem a bit less practical to some than worshiping your field god, but it's still widespread. A good analogy to this would be Egyptian Gods like Shu and Tefnut. These Gods were very important - they created the universe and were invoked in prayers and magic throughout the early and middle dynasties. However, they were not embraced by political or religious figure of the time so they didn't have the type of direct influence on affairs that the 'God of the Day' (which rotated according to the needs of the elite) did.<br /> <br /> In effect, they were very high Gods indeed. Almost like Godly grandparents, they were not as directly relevant as deities like Ra or Sutekh, but remained respected and worshiped nontheless. I see a very similar situation existing with the modern Immaculate Faith and the UCS.<br /> <br /> The Immaculates, it must be remembered, love the UCS and do not equate the actions of the Exalted that stole his energy with him. The UCS is the august emperor of heaven ; the 'Solar Exalted' are a bunch of demonologists that summoned up Ligier and traded some fellatio for Immense Cosmic Power. They hate one but worship the other and it's not a contradiction.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T09:50:56-07:00","id":1119007,"title":"","content":"A question is also what is required for something to count as a &quot;pray&quot; so it gives fuel to gods and Primordials. After all, it might be that every little thought counts. As things like the sun and the moon tend to pass through our minds fairly often, consider how often it would pass through the minds of those in a pre-industrial age. That trickle from each individual would be quite a torrent at when combined.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;god of the west field of the village, south of the hill&quot; would still not get much unless time is spent on some dedicated prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T10:08:39-07:00","id":1119014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1118970#post1118970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The UCS is one of the most widely worshiped Gods in Creation. The Immaculate Order worships him as a primary deity, confusing as that is.<br /> <br /> Most Solar Exalted who are exposed to the 'church of the UCS' are going to come into contact with the corrupted Immaculate interpretation first. Obviously, given the unique flavor of this interpretation, they may reject the notion that they have 'stolen' power from anything (particularly if they are Zenith).<br /> <br /> However, if one can somehow manage to discard the stuff about calling up demons to steal celestial energy, the UCS in the Immaculate Faith is more or less the same God that was worshiped in the mother culture prior to the Contagion and prior to the Shogunate. It's very likely that key details and aspects of that faith which survive are more or less accurate.<br /> <br /> The worship of the UCS might seem a bit less practical to some than worshiping your field god, but it's still widespread. A good analogy to this would be Egyptian Gods like Shu and Tefnut. These Gods were very important - they created the universe and were invoked in prayers and magic throughout the early and middle dynasties. However, they were not embraced by political or religious figure of the time so they didn't have the type of direct influence on affairs that the 'God of the Day' (which rotated according to the needs of the elite) did.<br /> <br /> In effect, they were very high Gods indeed. Almost like Godly grandparents, they were not as directly relevant as deities like Ra or Sutekh, but remained respected and worshiped nontheless. I see a very similar situation existing with the modern Immaculate Faith and the UCS.<br /> <br /> The Immaculates, it must be remembered, love the UCS and do not equate the actions of the Exalted that stole his energy with him. The UCS is the august emperor of heaven ; the 'Solar Exalted' are a bunch of demonologists that summoned up Ligier and traded some fellatio for Immense Cosmic Power. They hate one but worship the other and it's not a contradiction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Immaculate order recognizes the Sun as an entity from which power can be stolen from (like the moon). The Order, to my understanding, only worships deities on the specific feast days. I am curious to the notion that the UCS is primary in anyway, compared to the position the Immaculates take on the philosphical dragons (Who are emmulated not worshiped). I've also not heard or read of them paying particular reverence to him. My understanding, from House of The Bull God and comments from old dev <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/09/15/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-2/\" target=\"_blank\">team</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>The MG</i>:<br /> 1: Is the Unconquered Sun a known divinity, like in 2e, or a forgotten one, like in (early) 1e?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> 1: The Unconquered Sun has been forgotten.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><br /> <br /> Is that the UCS is no longer the most highly worshiped, or worshiped at all except at the edges of civilization (farther down the page).</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:59:11-07:00","id":1119114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119007#post1119007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question is also what is required for something to count as a &quot;pray&quot; so it gives fuel to gods and Primordials. After all, it might be that every little thought counts. As things like the sun and the moon tend to pass through our minds fairly often, consider how often it would pass through the minds of those in a pre-industrial age. That trickle from each individual would be quite a torrent at when combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut the Exalted can get Cults as well. If Sidereals or members of the Wyld Hunt think about you, does that qualify as worship?<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, since Cult is now solely about Willpower rather than Essence, even mortal humans, possibly even animals, can benefit from being worshipped.<br /> <br /> Mind, the corebook also establishes a variety of models for how Cults work. Fakharu's, for instance, consists in large part of tithes from his subordinates.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, while I do think that it's best not to get too hung up on the specifics of what constitutes prayer past the first dot, I'd say that it has to be a bit more than a bit of passive observation; some degree of veneration is required, even if it can come in a variety of forms.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the Unconquered Sun specifically, I would say that a number of factors mean that across the world, he has more worshippers than even he would know about (or even they would realize), if only from the lingering remnants of the large scope of his original worship. It possibly pales in comparison to the tithe of worship he's entitled to from all other Celestial gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T17:22:11-07:00","id":1119118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119114#post1119114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut the Exalted can get Cults as well. If Sidereals or members of the Wyld Hunt think about you, does that qualify as worship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible. But what would a couple of thousand thinking about you matter, compared to a few hundreds devouting their thoughts (praying) or several millions just thinking. Just in a way where thoughts are like the moist in the air, while dedicated prayers are a spring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:11:56-07:00","id":1119169,"title":"","content":"Exhibit P: Perfect Soul. <br /> <br /> Our new signature Zenith's pilgrimage to seek help from the gods in her threshold kingdom ended at a forlorn temple to the Unconquered Sun. <i>Unattended </i>and all but forgotten, it had surviving the weathering of the Second Age solely by being a manse build from jade and granite. Perfect Soul was exalted in an act of righteous indignation; <i>demolishing </i>the altar statue. Her Visitation informed her the Sun God was turning his face back towards Creation, and instructed her to use the empowerment to bring righteousness to the world as best she could. However, I still would not say that she <i>exactly </i>worships the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T06:08:42-07:00","id":1119236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119118#post1119118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible. But what would a couple of thousand thinking about you matter, compared to a few hundreds devouting their thoughts (praying) or several millions just thinking. Just in a way where thoughts are like the moist in the air, while dedicated prayers are a spring.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is one of those examples in which I think that this level of granularity doesn't really work. The Cult Merit is too straightforward, it doesn't accommodate questions of how it works when a certain subset of a Direction is especially dedicated compared to the more casual, even perfunctory worshippers.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the subject of the Unconquered Sun's obscurity, I had an amusing thought about how it would likely be something contrary to the usual assumption of the setting being driven by the Great Man Theory.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was thinking about factors that would drive such obscurity, and how I wouldn't find it very credible for them to come directly from any given agenda. I thought of the idea of it coming from the schemes of the Sidereals, which was immediately quashed by the sense that they wouldn't have the audacity. From there I got the sense that <i>nobody</i> would be so bold, assuming they necessarily had the will to try (I somewhat doubt the early Immaculates cared).<br /> <br /> \u200bSo from there I got the impression that worship of the Sun would fall out of fashion not because anybody specifically discouraged it, but as an emergent property of changes in the social context. Breakdowns in the Second Age changed the incentives behind why people worship in the first place, and alter the market of what gods are at work, and eventually you get a scenario in which worshipping the Sun is something that hardly anybody has the time or attention for. Eventually, the lack of reiterated attention means that you simply get generations of people who grow up with references to the Most High sun god being something they occasionally hear from their grandparents, at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:19:44-07:00","id":1119251,"title":"","content":"I was just reading the posts Epee102 quoted. It's <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/09/15/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-2/\" target=\"_blank\">somewhere around here</a>, about half of the way down. I'll make a copypasta of them (spoiled so as not to take a whole page):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>The MG</i>:<br /> 1: Is the Unconquered Sun a known divinity, like in 2e, or a forgotten one, like in (early) 1e?<br /> 2: Do Dragon-Blooded have any particular affinity with \u201cAspect-appropriate\u201d Evocations, or can you have a Daughter of Mela rocking out with Volcano Cutter, no questions asked?<br /> 3: Can you name something Solar Resistance does that it did not do before?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> 1: The Unconquered Sun has been forgotten.<br /> 2: They\u2019re all good with jade. All jade.<br /> 3: It can leech momentum from an attacker\u2019s ineffective strikes, cause their defense to topple on a bad hit, prevent you from taking killing damage when momentum is on your side, and it can turn you into an unstoppable killing machine for brief periods of time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Anaximander</i>:<br /> I find that\u2026 strange. I mean, of all the most obvious things to worship, the sun is right up there. I can\u2019t see people all through Creation just shrugging at the big bright thing up there, while worshiping the local spirit of butterflies, say. Does this mean that the Maidens and Luna are forgotten, too? Because, if they\u2019re worshiping the moon and the stars, but not the sun, that\u2019s REALLY weird. And though I know the bureaucracy of Heaven is being deemphasized, I find it hard to see the Immaculate Doctrine getting official support if it cuts out worship entirely to the King of Heaven, no matter how distracted and uninterested he is.<br /> But perhaps you mean that no one worships \u201cThe Unconquered Sun\u201d anymore, but, like \u201cRa the Sun-God of The Realm\u201d or such. But that raises all kinds of other questions, like, are these gods real spirits with a place in the Heavenly hierarchy? If so, Game aside, why would the UC allow usurpers to his domain? If there aren\u2019t any of these gods, how has the faith in them not been fulfilled?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Holden</i>:<br /> Which of these things actually responds to their prayers?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> There are a lot of possible reasons for your confusion, perhaps too many to suss out. I suggest you check out 1e\u2019s take on the Unconquered Sun, because that\u2019s the course EX3 has followed.<br /> As a side note: The Unconquered Sun still gets a % of all the prayers to every god \u201cunder the sun\u201d so to speak. He could never hear another prayer and still have more spiritual income than Ahlat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Lea</i>:<br /> Keep in mind that for most of history, the definition of faith was not \u201cBelief without evidence\u201d but rather \u201cTrust,\u201d hence statements like \u201cKeeping faith\u201d as synonymous with \u201cHonoring your agreements.\u201d Much of religion was and is about keeping faith with some figure in exchange for that figure\u2019s consideration.<br /> Creation\u2019s savants are aware of the Unconquered Sun as a mythic figure from the past, hence Perfect Soul having an altar to Him in some dusty, unattended portion of Jiara\u2019s ancient temple complex. But they have not kept faith with him, nor he with them, for a long, long time. To the extent people think of him at all, he\u2019s a mystery of the ancients, some god worshiped long ago and since forgotten. Did he even ever really exist?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Cadwyn</i>:<br /> So, sorta similar to how the Greek gods are known about intellectually today, but aren\u2019t formally worshiped and are seen purely as cultural and mythological history, to the degree that seeing someone building a temple and sacrificing to Zeus would turn heads and make you question their sanity.<br /> \u2026 and then some gal shows up, beats up a bear, and proclaims herself the daughter of Zeus. Yup, I think I have a pretty clear idea of how the average citizen of Creation might react to Solars.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Lea</i>:<br /> Not quite, no, because we grow up in a society where you learn about the Greek gods from picture-books in Kindergarten, or animated Disney movies. We have affection for the idea of the Greek gods, or the Norse gods, or the Egyptian gods, because they\u2019re icons from our childhood.<br /> Creation isn\u2019t a place where children are raised with that sort of broad multicultural knowledge base. The idea of worship of lost gods out of the past isn\u2019t something they can contextualize in terms of eccentric people who\u2019ve gotten too much into the picture-books.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Anaximander</i>:<br /> If no one worships him, though, despite the tithe of ambrosia he gets, how has the Unconquered Sun not just gone puff, or become the ultimate unemployed god? How has another sun god not risen (har har) in his place? I can understand \u201cThe Unconquered Sun\u201d no longer being worshiped because he does crap all for his worshipers, but not suddenly no one worshiping the Sun in all of Creation. And if other gods have sort of glommed the sun domain, how has he not risen in anger from the Jade Pleasure Dome between moves to smite such affront to his dignity?<br /> I fully trust and \u201chave faith\u201d in you guys, BTW. I just can\u2019t quite get my head around this one.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> Well, that\u2019s not what I said at all. I was answering a question with specific context. The person who asked it seemed to understand it. To clarify, though, he is an unknown because worship of and knowledge of him is suppressed, because at some point his 300 avatars ruled the entire world and all of the Exalted, and this is something the powers that be want swept under the rug. It\u2019s not that there\u2019s no sun worship, it\u2019s that the Unconquered Sun, King of Heaven, has been \u201cforgotten.\u201d That doesn\u2019t mean that nobody at all knows about him. Obviously, the Sidereals work in Yu-Shan and sometimes see him. This is just one example.<br /> The \u201cline\u201d on it is that he has been forgotten. Ie, the person asking the question, is he forgotten \u201clike in early 1e\u201d (as per the original question) where he was only worshiped by disparate barbarian madmen far outside the scope of the civilized nations or the \u201cknown world\u201d and this all goes back to the tone of 1e and the question I was answering.<br /> Hope that helps.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <i>Ardynor</i>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Oh really.<br /> Did he godspear Thorns yet? Did he erase any other shadowlands? Did he beat back the Wyld?<br /> No. He is sitting as impassively in heaven as he was. The solars are cycling and doing what they want without asking him. Their massed re-emergence has nothing at all to do with him.<br /> How at all is he different from back when he turned away from the world?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> The Exalted rule Creation. The Unconquered Sun sent back the Solars. The answer is right in front of you. The return of the Solars means more than everything you just suggested.<br /> \u201cTheir massed re-emergence has nothing at all to do with him.\u201d 2e was outlined to specifically contradict this assertion, and every single writer on the line until Glories ignored it. Many did the 180 degree opposite, which is why you see some dissonance in what we are saying as to what you have seen.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>ADamiani</i>:<br /> Ew.<br /> Kind of undercuts the whole Sol-is-a-dick thing.<br /> *sigh*<br /> I liked him better as the boss villain of the setting.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Lea</i>:<br /> Undercutting Sol-is-a-dick is deliberate. That was only funny when it wasn\u2019t receiving explicit textual support; a lot of the setting became less interesting when \u201cIt would really be funny if this were true\u201d became \u201cBecause it would be really funny if this were true, this should be made true.\u201d Lulz is no the highest aspiration of art and mankind, no matter what EncyclopediaDramatica says. The Unconquered Sun\u2019s dickishness or non-dickishness is meat to be ambivalent, with support for people who want to play it either way.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <i>John</i>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">In response to questions about the Unconquered Sun:<br /> He has begun Exalting Solars again. He is choosing heroes to drive back the darkness, bring order to chaos, and bring Creation back from the brink of doom. This may all be part of a larger plan on the part of the King of Heaven, or the plan may begin and end at \u201cit\u2019s in your hands now. Go forth and bring righteousness to the world as you see fit.\u201d It is up to the Storytellers to decide which will happen.<br /> That the Unconquered Sun has turned his face back to Creation is a huge, huge deal, even if he stays off camera for the duration of EX3\u2019s publication. The difference being that the Solar PCs could actually gain his endorsement, his favor, or his benefaction. If his face was turned away, they could not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Ardynor</i>:<br /> So which one is it? Are they independent or are they not? Honestly the only satisfactory tie in for both of those I see is if \u201cturning his face onto creation\u201d meant that he got off his bum and made a new batch of solars.<br /> And are you discarding the plot point of deathlord machinations breaking the prison and capturing only a portion of exaltations to turn into abyssals and infernals? If so, where would those types even come from?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Lea</i>:<br /> You\u2019re thinking of the Unconquered Sun as a big dude who does things the way people do. That is how most of the gods of the setting work; it\u2019s not necessarily how the Incarnae work.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>John</i>:<br /> Indeed. One need not think of the Unconquered Sun\u2019s Exaltations as independent of him, just because they are as unstoppable and inexorable in their efforts to \u201cchoose\u201d as the Sun is in his efforts to play the Games of Divinity.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><br /> <br /> So, TL;DR: UCS has definitely been forgotten (Epee102 and Greyman are absolutely correct). He's a mysterious figure from the ancient past, if you even know he was actually worshipped at some point. &quot;Did he even really exist?&quot;. He doesn't (usually?) answer prayers, not like your field god and river god might do. Worship and knowledge of him are suppressed, since The Powers That Be (the Realm and the Sidereals, I believe?) don't want it to be known his Chosen ruled the world and were slaughtered all. This doesn't mean the sun isn't worshipped, but people don't know much, if anything, about <i>the Unconquered Sun</i> himself. As others have pointed out in this thread, the sun might be linked to other gods in the worshippers' minds, or even to none. <i>There are</i> some who worship him in the present day, but they're the exception rather than the rule. He still receives more spiritual income than even major, contemporarily-worshipped gods by tithes alone, anyways.<br /> <br /> As for the Solars coming back - yes, they're back because the Jade Prison crashed, <i>and</i> because he's turned his face again toward Creation and has sent them back, choosing them. The two aren't mutually exclusive because he's a Celestial Incarna and the King of Heaven. He works in mysterious ways. Individual STs can decide whether he has further plans or the plan is <i>the Solars</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course individual STs can also decide that canon doesn't make sense to them, or they don't like it, and give a different spin to the whole matter, from how many people worship him in the modern day to what's actually happening with the Solars. This is the default.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to correct my assumptions if you feel I misrepresented the devs' answers.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T09:05:59-07:00","id":1119260,"title":"","content":"I admit, I never really understood the, &quot;Did he ever really exist?&quot; part.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order teaches that the Solar Anathema stole their power from the Unconquered Sun. And they <i>definitely</i> teach that the Solar Anathema exist (in fact, spreading word of the danger of the Solar and Lunar Exalted is arguably one of the most important things that the Immaculate monks do). Having a policy that would lead people to question, &quot;Well if the Unconquered Sun wasn't ever real, then maybe the Solar Anathema aren't real either, since how could they have stolen power from someone who never even existed?&quot; seems like it would undercut one of the most important facets of the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> My own take is that that most people in Creation (or at least those who have heard of the Solar Anathema, which would be most people) would at least know that there was some powerful sun god who existed in the past, from whom the Solar Anathema stole their power and some people might know the name of that deity. But I imagine that a lot of people in Creation simply assume that the Unconquered Sun died when the Solar Anathema stole their power from him - that's why he never answers prayers or does anything, because he's dead.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order either takes this as the official stance - that he was killed long ago by the Solar Anathema and no longer matters, or that they just don't bother correcting people who assume he died, because while the fact that he existed is important in relation to the existence of the Solar Anathema, his current state of existence is not important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-22-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T09:46:11-07:00","id":1119271,"title":"","content":"Ancient Roman historiography and mythology held that the city was founded by a man named Romulus, and you found even third century Romans expressing scepticism that he was actually real.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpeaking as a... let's say theist, I don't think that atheists find themselves doubting the existence of the world just because they don't believe in theistic historical narratives for the creation of the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, there's an amusing kind of multi-layered begging the question there; it's begging the question by presuming the existence of people <i>who are begging the question</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:24:56-07:00","id":1119278,"title":"","content":"In my games, pretty much everyone knows the Incarnae exist. &quot;My&quot; take on the Immaculate Faith/Philosophy describes them explicitly as the Rulers of Heaven, and those who gave the Exalted the Creation-Ruling Mandate. (which is, to various shades of interpretation, true, both in-universe and in-book)<br /> <br /> The proscription of Incarna-worship is much like the proscription of 'regular' deity veneration, except intensified to the nth degree. It would be <i>hilariously</i> heretical to publicly venerate the Incarnae, outside of extremely-narrow circumstances, and even then they are seen more as patrons of things than gods to be worshiped. Chances are, you overwhelmingly-likely won't see a shrine to one of the Incarnae, but instead a shrine to the actual god of the thing in question.<br /> <br /> The reasoning on that is simple: they are <u>busy</u>, indescribably so, and it would be <i>hilariously</i> presumptive to try and distract them with veneration and prayers, which could much-more-easily be directed to their subordinate deities.<br /> <br /> Generally, the Incarnae are viewed/described more like <i>Yahweh-</i>style overdeities than the 'regular' gods. <br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> -Mercury is invoked whenever a new road is built, or a port is opened..... but the road/port is dedicated to the road/harbor-gods, not Her<br /> <br /> -Venus is invoked during weddings, or when a child is born..... but the temple the wedding happens in is likely dedicated to another deity, not to Her<br /> <br /> -Mars is invoked when organized military forces are raised, or when a campaign is undertaken ..... but offerings are made to the regional war-gods, not to Her<br /> <br /> -Jupiter is invoked when universities, libraries, or other repositories of knowledge are built (She is often viewed as the patron of knowledge/intelligence in general, as opposed to 'just' secrets).... but the repository is going to be dedicated to other deities of learning and somesuch, not Her.<br /> <br /> - Saturn is invoked at funerals and such..... but cemeteries and other resting-places of the dead are dedicated to other deities, not Her.<br /> <br /> - Luna is ..... complicated. She is viewed as the patron of not only wilderness in general, but also hunting, fertility, sorcery, mysticism, and many, <i><u>many</u></i> other aspects of life. She is both the most 'well-known' Incarna, and the most-likely one to have actual worshipers. In my games, most 'barbarian' cultures across Creation venerate some aspect of Luna, which often causes them trouble when dealing with Immaculate 'civilized' folk.<br /> <br /> - Sol is ..... also complicated. Unlike both the rulebook and other people's interpretation of Him , He is <i>known about</i>, at the very least, across most of Creation, just not invoked for very much. He might be associated with agriculture, but not commonly. This is due to how His 'turning from Creation' is comparatively well-known in my games, unlike &quot;vanilla&quot; Creation, usually as an Immaculate Parable.<br /> <br /> - Gaia is almost-completely unknown. Most of her domains get folded into Luna's perview. Scholarly-types might know the name 'Gaia', but more as the fancy name for Creation than the name of a Ican'tbelieveShe'snotanIncarna.<br /> <br /> Yet again, Luna is <i>by far</i> the Incarna most likely to be venerated. She is also the one most likely to actually come down and visit Creation, in several aspects, and is the most humanlike and approachable.<br /> <br /> Both Solar and Lunar Anathema are known about, Lunars comparatively more so, and the existence of a third 'type' of Anathema is posited by scholarly-types; those who stole the power of the Maidens of Fate. Those who point this out are almost-always shut down by the argument 'where are they, then?&quot; No Fate-Anathema have ever appeared, so the argument appears to be moot.....<br /> <br /> The <u>existence</u> of Anathema is usually correlated by how much the Incarnae interact with Creation, and is usually used as yet another Immaculate Parable on why the Gods should mind their own business. Luna appears the most, allowing the Anathema to steal Her power most often, so most Anathema are Lunar. Sol interacted with Creation also, at least until He turned his face from it, so Solar Anathema are the second-most 'common'. The Maidens of Fate have apparently never interacted with Creation, giving the Anathema no chance to steal their powers, so there are accordingly no Fate-Anathema.<br /> <br /> Of course, the recent resurgence of Solar Anathema has led to a mass &quot;OH SHIT&quot; and much hand-flailing among scholarly-types in the know...... but also, oddly enough, a glimmer of hope. Does the appearance of the Solar Anathema mean Sol has turned His face back to Creation? Not that it means very much......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:38:09-07:00","id":1119283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119271#post1119271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancient Roman historiography and mythology held that the city was founded by a man named Romulus, and you found even third century Romans expressing scepticism that he was actually real.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, if you had a bunch of super magical dudes walking around with Magical Rome Powers and the largest religion having it as a foundational point to make sure that everyone know how scary these guys were and that they had stolen their powers from Romulus, and then if there were also super scary dudes with Magical Carthage Powers and that same religion made it clear that they had stolen their powers from Dido, you might have seen a bit less skepticism over the existence of Romulus.<br /> <br /> It's known in Creation that gods can be hurt and killed (the fact that Immaculate Monks can hurt and kill spirits is not some kind of high level secret and probably makes for popular stories), and it's widely believed that the Solar Anathema stole their powers from the god of the sun. I imagine it's much more common for people to believe that the sun god died a long time ago, than to believe that there was never a sun god in the first place and that the Solar Anathema just kind of showed up one day whole cloth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:11:21-07:00","id":1119295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119283#post1119283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, if you had a bunch of super magical dudes walking around with Magical Rome Powers and the largest religion having it as a foundational point to make sure that everyone know how scary these guys were and that they had stolen their powers from Romulus, and then if there were also super scary dudes with Magical Carthage Powers and that same religion made it clear that they had stolen their powers from Dido, you might have seen a bit less skepticism over the existence of Romulus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to reference things about the Flat Earth Society, but while it does represent a rather pertinent (and uncontroversial) example of people believing in a thing in contravention of the most basic available facts, it doesn't quite cover the same ground as this.<br /> <br /> \u200bBasically, I still find your reasoning to be flawed. The existence of a thing in no way implies that popular narratives about the thing are necessarily correct. This example you're positing here? Of people with magical Rome powers associated with a mythology presenting them as something that was stolen from an ancient culture hero? It is <i>still</i> begging the question. It is still assuming that the existence of capabilities like this is unthinkable without an explanation such as that. Hell, it would not be irrefutable even if the iconography of such powers were very heavily tailored to emulate the popular imagery of that culture hero, because who's to say that the powers did not originate under circumstances that were intended to give that impression? Scepticism in such a case is perfectly reasonable, and corroboration requires much higher standards of evidence.<br /> <br /> What do you think the field of archaeology is about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's known in Creation that gods can be hurt and killed (the fact that Immaculate Monks can hurt and kill spirits is not some kind of high level secret and probably makes for popular stories), and it's widely believed that the Solar Anathema stole their powers from the god of the sun. I imagine it's much more common for people to believe that the sun god died a long time ago, than to believe that there was never a sun god in the first place and that the Solar Anathema just kind of showed up one day whole cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat is a false dichotomy; people can believe in more elaborate origins for the Anathema even if they don't think any given Incarna ever existed.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's also a fallacy in any given presentation that says that because some gods are known to exist, people ought to believe that every god who is ever referred to must exist, especially the ones who conveniently cloistered themselves off in a building in the inaccessible spirit realm for the past several centuries.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Hell, one plausible alternative narrative for somebody to believe in is that the Anathema figured out powers that made them all golden and shiny, and then <i>they</i> were the ones who made up the Unconquered Sun as a way of legitimizing themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-22-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:26:57-07:00","id":1119300,"title":"","content":"It's been 1500 years, 90% of everyone died halfway through, and the world's largest government, its main religion, and the people who practically run Heaven and fate itself all want inconvenient parts of history to disappear. It's a miracle they still remember anything at all.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though... one thing available to Solars, especially Zeniths, is to tell a story about how you restore worship of the UCS to the world. There's this really dumb Christian Evangelical narrative where they assume that whoever they're trying to convert has never heard of Christ before (you see this in eg. Chick Tracts all the time, &quot;tell me more about this 'Jesus' person!&quot;) - it makes no sense in modern America, but it endures because it makes for a good story.<br /> <br /> So Exalted is designed to set it up, to put your Zenith in a position where they can reveal the good news of the UCS to people who've forgotten it and play a holy-roller revivalist.<br /> <br /> For that to work, he has to be mostly (but not <i>quite</i> entirely) forgotten. Hence, the bits about how the Sidereals and Immaculate Faith work to minimize him, but are too worried about offending him to actively suppress everything about him completely. Bits and pieces survive, enough so you can sell his narrative to unbelievers without it sounding like you're talking crazy-talk, but with enough twisted or lost or forgotten that you're still delivering the Good News to people who will react with gasps to this idea of a human-friendly king of heaven who cares about them personally.<br /> <br /> (Yes, yes, I know. But that's how you frame it as a Zenith. Theological and practical doubts about the UCS are something else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:46:40-07:00","id":1119306,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11892\" data-vbnamecard=\"11892\">Boston123</a> has neat thoughts. I agree with Boston123.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T12:42:39-07:00","id":1119321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119295#post1119295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere's also a fallacy in any given presentation that says that because some gods are known to exist, people ought to believe that every god who is ever referred to must exist, especially the ones who conveniently cloistered themselves off in a building in the inaccessible spirit realm for the past several centuries.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Hell, one plausible alternative narrative for somebody to believe in is that the Anathema figured out powers that made them all golden and shiny, and then <i>they</i> were the ones who made up the Unconquered Sun as a way of legitimizing themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the largest and most influential religion in Creation teaches that there is/was a sun god whom the Solar Anathema stole their power from, and that the Lunar Anthema stole their power from the moon god. So most people who follow the Immaculate religion (which is a pretty substantial segment of Creation's population) are probably going to believe that. And even among those who don't follow the Immaculate Philosophy, most of them recognize the teachings about the Solar and Lunar Anathema. This is why places of safe harbor for Lunars and Solars are extremely rare in Creation, even in places where the Immaculate Philosophy is not the dominant religion.<br /> <br /> It just seems unlikely to me that most people in Creation would feel that the Immaculate Philosophy's ideas on the Anathema are inaccurate when the gameline has generally tried to show that the teachings of the Immaculate Philosophy (especially in regard to the Anathema) are pretty widespread and accepted.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* There are, undoubtedly, some parts of Creation where they laugh at what the Immaculate Order teaches, and indeed there may even be places that have never heard of the Solars or Lunars before in the first place. But I would hazard that in most of Creation, what the Immaculate Order teaches about the Anathema is widely accepted, and that includes the idea that there was a sun deity whom the Solars stole their powers from. Places that have never heard of this or that flatly reject it would probably be in the definite minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-22-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T14:17:36-07:00","id":1119336,"title":"","content":"I would also add, regarding Solars specifically worshipping the UCS:<br /> <br /> Exalted <i>generally</i> treats Exaltation as a spiritual event, not just a powerup. Yes, a lot of people just believe what they were raised as, but sometimes people experience some sort of spiritual awakening that makes them change their views, especially in stories. And Exaltation is very much intended to be that sort of thing. Not for <i>everyone</i>, but I think the assertion that a majority of Zeniths end up worshiping the UCS is not unwarranted - it's supposed to be that sort of thing. It's not just the UCS dropping in to give you a message, it's a transcendent life-altering spiritual experience, and I think it's reasonable to say that for many people a distant mostly-cultural faith in a distant god they never saw any hint of cannot really compete with that.<br /> <br /> (And also that most of the people who view their faith as a purely cultural thing with no spiritual dimension to it would probably not end up as Zeniths in the first place.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-22-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T16:00:08-07:00","id":1119354,"title":"","content":"Maybe related to that idea, I was thinking earlier in the thread about the degree to which Solars becoming most puissant in their Charms and cultivated in their Essence is one and the same as becoming spiritually closer to, or at least more understanding of, the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> (Thought spurred in the context of Jen talking about Solars becoming less religious as they become more experienced, although I know he was talking more about their world experience and experience of Creation's world religions).<br /> <br /> Be interested to know anyone's thoughts on that. Is it an accurate or plausible read of the world described by the setting? What are the pros and cons for games and stories? <br /> <br /> (I was thinking if anything it may be slightly contentious out of the idea that Solars should be &quot;free&quot; to become more powerful as Solars while becoming more spiritually alienated from the Sun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T20:15:05-07:00","id":1119388,"title":"","content":"For an example of how the restoration of the UCS to a primal position in people's lives might work, I would recommend the story of Samurai Jack and Ashi. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ashi starts out as a committed worshipper of Aku/devoted follower of the Immaculate Order, then is sent out on a mission of assassination/Wyld Hunt against the samurai/a Solar Exalted. Her sisters/the rest of the Hunt die in the process, but she survives. The samurai/Solar keeps her with him, and eventually convinces her that she's been on the wrong side, mostly by being a decent person.</div></div> </div> </div>Frankly, if your Creation doesn't allow for such things, I think it's a rotten setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-23-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T02:36:22-07:00","id":1119440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119321#post1119321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, the largest and most influential religion in Creation teaches that there is/was a sun god whom the Solar Anathema stole their power from, and that the Lunar Anthema stole their power from the moon god. So most people who follow the Immaculate religion (which is a pretty substantial segment of Creation's population) are probably going to believe that. And even among those who don't follow the Immaculate Philosophy, most of them recognize the teachings about the Solar and Lunar Anathema. This is why places of safe harbor for Lunars and Solars are extremely rare in Creation, even in places where the Immaculate Philosophy is not the dominant religion.<br /> <br /> It just seems unlikely to me that most people in Creation would feel that the Immaculate Philosophy's ideas on the Anathema are inaccurate when the gameline has generally tried to show that the teachings of the Immaculate Philosophy (especially in regard to the Anathema) are pretty widespread and accepted.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* There are, undoubtedly, some parts of Creation where they laugh at what the Immaculate Order teaches, and indeed there may even be places that have never heard of the Solars or Lunars before in the first place. But I would hazard that in most of Creation, what the Immaculate Order teaches about the Anathema is widely accepted, and that includes the idea that there was a sun deity whom the Solars stole their powers from. Places that have never heard of this or that flatly reject it would probably be in the definite minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't wanna seem stubborn, but, I dunno, I just re-read the sections about the Immaculate Philosophy in the core book, and it doesn't talk about teachings of a sun god or a moon god (and why should it? The Immaculate Dragons are the focus of the faith, and spiritual perfection through multiple reincarnations, not &quot;bureaucrat gods&quot; the common people shouldn't even worship...).<br /> <br /> It appears the Anathema are mainly known as just that, Anathema, referring primarily to Lunars, secondarily to Solars, and then to Abyssals, Liminals and Exigents (and if convenient, Fair Folk, elementals, beastmen, demons... as long as you're not with them, you're against them). But the adherents don't usually make a distinction, and even less wonder from whom or what the Anathema stole their powers, if at all - most people just know how to identify an anathema - golden or silver light, mainly - and that, when in doubt, they should run and fetch a monk.<br /> <br /> Have the devs talked about how the Immaculates teach about the origin of the Anathema? Is it stated somewhere else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:40:50-07:00","id":1119447,"title":"","content":"I find that there is an exclusion of the idea of people who generally adhere to the Immaculate faith, but does not think every minute aspect of its teachings is literally true, either out of a general scepticism or thinking that some elements might be more metaphorical or analogous.<br /> <br /> Among other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The basic point is, it is positing a setting that is terribly lacking in nuance.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Anathema are feared, first and foremost, because of a long history of them doing terrifying things, not because of a just-so story that says they exist because they took power from some obscure deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:41:54-07:00","id":1119448,"title":"","content":"Oh dear, I hope I have not caught even the barest glimpse of an unmarked spoiler for Samurai Jack. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T08:48:20-07:00","id":1119528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119447#post1119447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that there is an exclusion of the idea of people who generally adhere to the Immaculate faith, but does not think every minute aspect of its teachings is literally true, either out of a general scepticism or thinking that some elements might be more metaphorical or analogous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are vastly underestimating how seriously people take religious writings. People in the real world often take their religious writings extremely literally and believe them to an incredibly high degree. Last time I checked, even today nearly half of Americans believe in a the literal Biblical account of the world's creation, flatly rejecting any idea that contradicts it. And, of course, if you were to go back in time to say, 10th century Europe you would find far, far more people taking the words of the Bible as literal truth.<br /> <br /> I never got the feeling that people in Creation are supposed to be more skeptical about their religious beliefs than people in the real world were. Rather, it's a setting in which people will sometimes engage in duels (to the death even!) over the minutiae of their religious texts and in which hammering home the truth of the Immaculate faith is one of the major goals of the Immaculate Order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:06:08-07:00","id":1119537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119528#post1119528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, even today nearly half of Americans believe in a the literal Biblical account of the world's creation, flatly rejecting any idea that contradicts it.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Half of Americans?!!</i> I dearly hope that piece of data is inaccurate...<br /> <br /> In other news, I made a mistake (so not really, <i>really</i> news). Spoilered for your convenience:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It appears the Immaculate Order <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/08/08/ask-the-developers-thread-summary/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>does</i> teach that the Anathema steal power from the Sun and the Moon</a>, specifically, quote:<br /> &quot;<i>AlphaWhelp</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">:</span></span> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You have to remember the definition of Anathema. Anathema does not, and has never meant Exalted that aren\u2019t Dragon-Blooded. It meant, more or less, that a demon has escaped hell, destroyed your childhood friend\u2019s soul, possessed him, and is trying to masquerade as him, but is really a hollow shell of a person, animated only by the possessing demon inside of them, and has access to the supernatural powers of that demon. Obviously this doesn\u2019t apply to Exigents since they are godly in nature and not demonic.<br /> <i>Lea</i>:<br /> Not so much a demon as the revenant spirit of an ancient sorcerer who made pacts with the Yozis to steal power from the Sun or Moon, but overall yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I still don't believe the Order teaches people about UCS, considering the fact he's been described as a forgotten god, many times, but yes, in orthodox Immaculate doctrine the Anathema are in fact &quot;revenant spirits of ancient sorcerers who made pacts with the Yozis to steal power from the Sun or Moon&quot; and who possess people.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.<br /> We now return you to your regularly scheduled programming.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:25:54-07:00","id":1119542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119537#post1119537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Half of Americans?!!</i> I dearly hope that piece of data is inaccurate...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. The number has been <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/210956/belief-creationist-view-humans-new-low.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">sharply plummeting of late</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:56:46-07:00","id":1119550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119542#post1119542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is. The number has been <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/210956/belief-creationist-view-humans-new-low.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">sharply plummeting of late</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still 38%?!! What do these people eat, bread and creationism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:06:18-07:00","id":1119554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119542#post1119542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. The number has been <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/210956/belief-creationist-view-humans-new-low.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">sharply plummeting of late</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh thanks, last time I saw the numbers (about 5 years ago) it was at around 47%, which is roughly half of Americans. Nice to see it's starting to decline, but we're still sitting at well over 1/3rd of Americans who believe in a strictly Biblical account of Creationism. And this is after decades of people attending public schools, learning about evolution, how the universe was created and other such things. Religious beliefs die hard, and I just don't imagine most people in Creation, especially those living in territories where it's the dominant religion, would be all that skeptical of the Immaculate religion's account of what occurred in the past (which again, notes that the Anathema stole their power from the sun god).<br /> <br /> The name of that sun god might be forgotten, but I have trouble that imagining that there is a huge contingent of people wondering, &quot;Did the sun god the Anathema stole their powers from ever even exist?&quot; Which is why I found the idea a little odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:21:28-07:00","id":1119558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119554#post1119554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh thanks, last time I saw the numbers (about 5 years ago) it was at around 47%, which is roughly half of Americans. Nice to see it's starting to decline, but we're still sitting at well over 1/3rd of Americans who believe in a strictly Biblical account of Creationism. And this is after decades of people attending public schools, learning about evolution, how the universe was created and other such things. Religious beliefs die hard, and I just don't imagine most people in Creation, especially those living in territories where it's the dominant religion, would be all that skeptical of the Immaculate religion's account of what occurred in the past (which again, notes that the Anathema stole their power from the sun god).<br /> <br /> The name of that sun god might be forgotten, but I have trouble that imagining that there is a huge contingent of people wondering, &quot;Did the sun god the Anathema stole their powers from ever even exist?&quot; Which is why I found the idea a little odd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might be more &quot;did the demon sorcerer anathema ever exist?&quot; <br /> Remember, only a few hundred lunars exist in all creation. Some followers may never have encountered them as more then boogeymen to frighten children and serve as examples of what not to be in life. <br /> Alternatively, did the sun god survive? Or since all his power was stolen, why worship him? After all, the Anathema now have it. Worship to him might give them power, somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/