div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It appears the Immaculate Order <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/08/08/ask-the-developers-thread-summary/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>does</i> teach that the Anathema steal power from the Sun and the Moon</a>, specifically, quote:<br /> &quot;<i>AlphaWhelp</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">:</span></span> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You have to remember the definition of Anathema. Anathema does not, and has never meant Exalted that aren\u2019t Dragon-Blooded. It meant, more or less, that a demon has escaped hell, destroyed your childhood friend\u2019s soul, possessed him, and is trying to masquerade as him, but is really a hollow shell of a person, animated only by the possessing demon inside of them, and has access to the supernatural powers of that demon. Obviously this doesn\u2019t apply to Exigents since they are godly in nature and not demonic.<br /> <i>Lea</i>:<br /> Not so much a demon as the revenant spirit of an ancient sorcerer who made pacts with the Yozis to steal power from the Sun or Moon, but overall yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I still don't believe the Order teaches people about UCS, considering the fact he's been described as a forgotten god, many times, but yes, in orthodox Immaculate doctrine the Anathema are in fact &quot;revenant spirits of ancient sorcerers who made pacts with the Yozis to steal power from the Sun or Moon&quot; and who possess people.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.<br /> We now return you to your regularly scheduled programming.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's less that they teach about the Ignis Divine and Luna and more they acknowledge the existence of them and that the two are powerful gods. That said they don't teach much beyond, &quot;Yes there are gods for the sun and moon, but it is best to leave matters concerning them and their favor to the clergy as they are powerful gods and could bring great ruin were someone offend them accidentally.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:18:57-07:00","id":1119664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119558#post1119558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It might be more &quot;did the demon sorcerer anathema ever exist?&quot;<br /> Remember, only a few hundred lunars exist in all creation. Some followers may never have encountered them as more then boogeymen to frighten children and serve as examples of what not to be in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA lot of Lunars are making a very visible spectacle of themselves. You don't need to have encountered them personally for the impact of their presence to be felt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:22:57-07:00","id":1119667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119528#post1119528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are vastly underestimating how seriously people take religious writings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which people?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll admit, I've been popping into this discussion only sporadically, so I don't know how this tangent started. I want to be clear that I am not operating under an assumption that everybody thinks that there is no Unconquered Sun. I am operating more along the lines of there being a certain line of inquiry among the intelligentsia.<br /> <br /> I would think that it would be clear that I, of all people, am not discussing anything in terms of non-existent universals.<br /> <br /> Nothing is true, everything is permitted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:40:31-07:00","id":1119674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119664#post1119664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bA lot of Lunars are making a very visible spectacle of themselves. You don't need to have encountered them personally for the impact of their presence to be felt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but the Solar exalted do less so (until lately), and I was thinking more along the lines of the second question then the first. I also wonder on the impact level through out the realm (I can imagine villages having never dealt with Lunars and not having been terribly impacted by them as far as they know. The increased taxation to pay for a greater millitary campaign might be perceived merely as increased taxation, for instance.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:13:18-07:00","id":1119686,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue I think is that Solars draw on a genre of heroism that is defined by being change-makers, which is contrary to the most prominent heroic fiction genre in modern media, as superheroes are overwhelmingly status-quo defenders. You see those tropes play out most strongly with the Alchemicals, who are generally presented in setting as righteously fitting in with the religious cultural values of their society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-25-2017, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:06:45-07:00","id":1119758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119528#post1119528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in the real world often take their religious writings extremely literally and believe them to an incredibly high degree. Last time I checked, even today nearly half of Americans believe in a the literal Biblical account of the world's creation, flatly rejecting any idea that contradicts it. And, of course, if you were to go back in time to say, 10th century Europe you would find far, far more people taking the words of the Bible as literal truth.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.reasons.org/articles/how-young-earth-creationism-became-a-core-tenet-of-american-fundamentalism-part-2\" target=\"_blank\">This is a far more recent idea than you're suggesting.</a> <a href=\"http://www.sciencemeetsreligion.org/theology/bible-inerrant.php\" target=\"_blank\">People from the <i>5th</i> century spoke of Genesis being allegorical. It was the Catholic Church's position at the time\u2026 and still is!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-24-2017, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T01:04:36-07:00","id":1119801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119667#post1119667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which people?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll admit, I've been popping into this discussion only sporadically, so I don't know how this tangent started. I want to be clear that I am not operating under an assumption that everybody thinks that there is no Unconquered Sun. I am operating more along the lines of there being a certain line of inquiry among the intelligentsia.<br /> <br /> I would think that it would be clear that I, of all people, am not discussing anything in terms of non-existent universals.<br /> <br /> Nothing is true, everything is permitted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the end of the day, if there is supposed to be a sense of atheism (or at least skepticism) towards the existence of a god of the sun, to the point that a large group of people doubt that the sun ever even had a god, that probably deserves a bit of detail in the books. Gods in Creation aren't unknowable mysteries but rather definite existences in the world. If you want to meet the god of the Imperial City, all you have to do is arrange a meeting with his secretary. Most people in Creation probably have a basic understanding that things have gods - that the river has a god, and the forest has a god, and the mountain has a god and that it's possible for those gods to actually do things. It seems odd that people would overly question whether the sun has a god when pretty much everything else does. This is in the same way that most people probably understand that black magic can make corpses walk again, the ghosts of dead people can return to the world or that Fair Folk can devour your soul.<br /> <br /> While, of course, people in Creation don't have access to the Exalted corebook, at the same time I can't imagine that there are all that many people in Creation who seriously consider Fair Folk or Ghosts or Gods (or the Exalted!) to be mere superstitious nonsense.<br /> <br /> If, when a Zenith rolls into town and starts talking about the god of the sun, a number of people laugh at the absurdity of the idea of the sun even having a god is not an uncommon response, then that's probably worth exploring in the books why and how this apparently singular belief about the lack of a sun god has come to pass, in a setting where it is going to be widely accepted that gods do, in fact, exist, that pretty much everything has a god and when the largest religious order in Creation specifically notes the fact that the sun does (or did) have a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T02:01:56-07:00","id":1119807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, if there is supposed to be a sense of atheism (or at least skepticism) towards the existence of a god of the sun, to the point that a large group of people doubt that the sun ever even had a god, that probably deserves a bit of detail in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss it? The existence of the supernatural does not preclude the existence of hucksters and fakers. Skepticism is a fairly healthy approach when someone wants to sell you a bridge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods in Creation aren't unknowable mysteries but rather definite existences in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they don't even have physical bodies unless they choose to manifest them. They are not-figuratively <i>immaterial</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to meet the god of the Imperial City, all you have to do is arrange a meeting with his secretary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something of an oversimplification. I highly doubt Gri-Fel will voluntarily meet with a grubby peasant (or even patrician!) just because his secretary penciled it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems odd that people would overly question whether the sun has a god when pretty much everything else does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it matter if something has a spirit if that spirit never does anything? Regardless of whether it's a grain of rice or the thing in the sky that lights the entire world, if its attendant spirit does not act, <i>it <b>effectively</b> does not have a god</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is in the same way that most people probably understand that black magic can make corpses walk again, the ghosts of dead people can return to the world or that Fair Folk can devour your soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that most people have never seen it themselves, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-24-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T04:09:56-07:00","id":1119833,"title":"","content":"The way I see it. Long ago when UCS was active in the world prior to the War and then during the first deliberative, it would not have been inconceivable for entire nations to honor him specifically and thus lots of iconography from that time bears the sun's image - but;<br /> <br /> On the turn of the age, when UCS turned his back on Creation and the deliberative was overthrown, all of mortal societies still worshiping him directly would have found their prayers unanswered or delegated to some other divine intermediary. So over thousands of years of no direct contact with the sun the lesser stations gained prominence as they were more immidiately accessible (and possibly willing to interfere) - this the decline of UCS worship is like a learned process over many generations which slowly reduces the iconography of the sun directly and leaves his dedicated temples empty. <br /> <br /> You'll still get fringe cases where some people still worship him directly, but either their prayers are never answered or (in the rare case of sufficient gravitas to require heavenly attention) superlative delegation has someone else showing up at your temple or (more likely) the problem is quietly fixed with no attribution to a being whatsoever. <br /> <br /> Couple all that with a deliberate project by the immaculate order and it's puppeteers to quash established worship as a religious tool unless your hands and soul are worthy enough, and the population of creation slowly veers away from the old brilliant god, still know he is there, but perhaps less immidiately relevant. Heaven is a bureau, after all, and even if you write a letter to the CEO, or President or whatever leader there may be, how likely is it, do you think, that they would even get to read it let alone know you sent it? On the off chance you get an answer, the letter is typed and a simulacrum of their signature is printed on the bottom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:08:16-07:00","id":1119875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119833#post1119833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it. Long ago when UCS was active in the world prior to the War and then during the first deliberative, it would not have been inconceivable for entire nations to honor him specifically and thus lots of iconography from that time bears the sun's image - but;<br /> <br /> On the turn of the age, when UCS turned his back on Creation and the deliberative was overthrown, all of mortal societies still worshiping him directly would have found their prayers unanswered or delegated to some other divine intermediary. So over thousands of years of no direct contact with the sun the lesser stations gained prominence as they were more immidiately accessible (and possibly willing to interfere) - this the decline of UCS worship is like a learned process over many generations which slowly reduces the iconography of the sun directly and leaves his dedicated temples empty.<br /> <br /> You'll still get fringe cases where some people still worship him directly, but either their prayers are never answered or (in the rare case of sufficient gravitas to require heavenly attention) superlative delegation has someone else showing up at your temple or (more likely) the problem is quietly fixed with no attribution to a being whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Couple all that with a deliberate project by the immaculate order and it's puppeteers to quash established worship as a religious tool unless your hands and soul are worthy enough, and the population of creation slowly veers away from the old brilliant god, still know he is there, but perhaps less immidiately relevant. Heaven is a bureau, after all, and even if you write a letter to the CEO, or President or whatever leader there may be, how likely is it, do you think, that they would even get to read it let alone know you sent it? On the off chance you get an answer, the letter is typed and a simulacrum of their signature is printed on the bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that that's the most plausible way to do it. When the Sun doesn't answer your prayers while the local forest goddess does (and sends wood spiders to attack your livestock if you don't pray to her), over time, people are just going to worship the Sun less and less.<br /> Plus, of course, the Immaculate Order gets upset over you worshipping local gods, but they get really upset over you worshipping the UCS.<br /> So... why bother.<br /> It's not that no-one <i>ever</i> worships him, there's probably small sun cults and so forth, it's just rare.<br /> <br /> And I'd guess forgotten means in the sense that maybe if you ask a scholar of religion, they might be able to tell you that the sun has a god called The Unconquered Sun, but your average peasant couldn't name him (whereas they probably could name the main gods worshipped by their culture, and some local terrestrial Gods). It's not that the idea of the Sun having a god is radically strange to them, it's just... well, who cares? It's not very important. He's the god of the sun, not the god of peasants.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:17:33-07:00","id":1119877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119758#post1119758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in the real world often take their religious writings extremely literally and believe them to an incredibly high degree. Last time I checked, even today nearly half of Americans believe in a the literal Biblical account of the world's creation, flatly rejecting any idea that contradicts it. And, of course, if you were to go back in time to say, 10th century Europe you would find far, far more people taking the words of the Bible as literal truth.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.reasons.org/articles/how-young-earth-creationism-became-a-core-tenet-of-american-fundamentalism-part-2\" target=\"_blank\">This is a far more recent idea than you're suggesting.</a> <a href=\"http://www.sciencemeetsreligion.org/theology/bible-inerrant.php\" target=\"_blank\">People from the <i>5th</i> century spoke of Genesis being allegorical. It was the Catholic Church's position at the time\u2026 and still is!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And 3rd century.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the Catholic Church had (and has) no official position on the literalism of Genesis. Medieval Christians generally weren't that fussed about how literal the Old Testament was, since they assumed virtually every single bit was symbolic of Jesus (they lived in a very symbolic society after all, which until the 12th century was relatively uninterested in how things actually physically worked), and that was the important bit.<br /> Though they were very keen that the universe literally had a beginning, and hadn't existed infinitely (because that's what a lot of Hellenic pagans argued).<br /> <br /> So, anyway, to get back to Exalted, I wouldn't assume they are as interested as we are in what is literally true. Our culture (well, this has been a rising theme since the early 18th century) is, in historical terms, one that's very focused on literal truth (though perhaps less since post-modernism).<br /> <br /> Not to say that I'd expect people in Exalted to live in an entirely symbolic way, but I'd expect them generally to be less interested in what is literally going on in Yu-Shan. The details of the Sun God might be an idle topic of conversation, or of interest to scholars, but it's not generally something your average peasant cares about. The sun works without prayer, so it's not something worth bothering about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-24-2017, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:24:05-07:00","id":1119881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119801#post1119801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If, when a Zenith rolls into town and starts talking about the god of the sun, a number of people laugh at the absurdity of the idea of the sun even having a god is not an uncommon response, then that's probably worth exploring in the books why and how this apparently singular belief about the lack of a sun god has come to pass, in a setting where it is going to be widely accepted that gods do, in fact, exist, that pretty much everything has a god and when the largest religious order in Creation specifically notes the fact that the sun does (or did) have a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there, I think that would be a bit odd. But I don't think it's what implied by &quot;the Unconquered Sun is a largely forgotten God.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd expect the local peasants to say &quot;okay, sure, the sun has a god I guess, but why is it important? He does his job of pushing the sun around, what's that got to do with us?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Which is probably something that a Zenith with performance charms isn't going to find that challenging to deal with.)<br /> <br /> Something that just occurred to me, although I guess it's quite obvious: Creation has tens of thousands of gods (or maybe millions, or billions? Not sure how much least gods are still a thing). Your average peasant can probably name like 20-30. So if you tell him the Sun God is called Ignis Divine, he's probably not going to be like &quot;what? How come I've never heard of him? That's so weird!&quot; He'll probably just be like &quot;oh, I didn't know that,&quot; and then forget it a week later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:34:37-07:00","id":1119888,"title":"","content":"I think the role of least gods is getting passed back to the pattern spiders, and even then only in the broadest sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:37:19-07:00","id":1119891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119888#post1119888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the role of least gods is getting passed back to the pattern spiders, and even then only in the broadest sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. I don't think they really added anything to the setting. To me, I found they mostly made gods feel... well, just not that exciting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T09:30:28-07:00","id":1119917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119891#post1119891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good. I don't think they really added anything to the setting. To me, I found they mostly made gods feel... well, just not that exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less that least gods are not a thing at all, and more that they aren't assumed to be so universal anymore. The Core has the god of a field statted, for instance, but that doesn't mean every field you come across will have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T09:57:50-07:00","id":1119924,"title":"","content":"A field god isn't a least god, at least not in the sense we mean. We're talking about the idea that every single blade of grass has its own god that popped up in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:03:20-07:00","id":1119927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119881#post1119881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you there, I think that would be a bit odd. But I don't think it's what implied by &quot;the Unconquered Sun is a largely forgotten God.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd expect the local peasants to say &quot;okay, sure, the sun has a god I guess, but why is it important? He does his job of pushing the sun around, what's that got to do with us?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was discussing Lea's remark in which he said that people would wonder if the sun ever even had a god in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Keep in mind that for most of history, the definition of faith was not \u201cBelief without evidence\u201d but rather \u201cTrust,\u201d hence statements like \u201cKeeping faith\u201d as synonymous with \u201cHonoring your agreements.\u201d Much of religion was and is about keeping faith with some figure in exchange for that figure\u2019s consideration.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Creation\u2019s savants are aware of the Unconquered Sun as a mythic figure from the past, hence Perfect Soul having an altar to Him in some dusty, unattended portion of Jiara\u2019s ancient temple complex. But they have not kept faith with him, nor he with them, for a long, long time. To the extent people think of him at all, he\u2019s a mystery of the ancients, some god worshiped long ago and since forgotten. Did he even ever really exist?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\">The statement simply struck me as a bit odd to me in a setting in which people know that gods do exist (if you want to open a salt mine and you make the local salt gods mad they are going to kill you), in which people know gods can be killed (the fact that Immaculate Monks can fight and kill gods is no secret) and in which the largest religious order in the world makes it a point of fact that the sun had a god whom the Anathema stole their powers from. I would think much more likely that most people would simply assume that the Unconquered Sun is a dead god, probably killed by the Anathema, rather a god who never even existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Or to put it another way, there are many conclusions one can take from the silence of the sun god - that he's dead or trapped away or what have you. But when the world's largest religion says that the sun god existed, and when gods of other things exist, it makes me wonder why people would jump to the conclusion that the sun never had a god to begin with.<br /> <br /> If there is a strong strain of atheism in Creation, and people commonly laugh at the idea of gods - &quot;Oh that forest doesn't have a god, don't be silly,&quot; or &quot;There is no god of the Imperial Mountain,&quot; or &quot;Salt gods? Don't be silly, they don't exist! Now get those miners back in there,&quot; then people coming to the conclusion that the sun never had a god to begin with either, despite the world's largest religion saying he exists, would make sense.<br /> <br /> But I never got the feeling that this was a terribly prevalent attitude towards the gods in Creation, and if it is then it's something that <i>definitely</i> needs to be explored in the books.For the most part the setting has presented gods as fairly common, and that their interaction with humanity isn't exactly rare or obscure (we have entire cities which are based around gods hanging out and doing stuff in physical form) so this attitude simply struck me as a bit unusual.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-24-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:15:34-07:00","id":1119934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119924#post1119924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A field god isn't a least god, at least not in the sense we mean. We're talking about the idea that every single blade of grass has its own god that popped up in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, yeah, no, that's taking it too far. A blade of grass <i>might</i> have a spirit overseeing it (for example, a Censor could've punished a god by demoting it to some menial task), but it probably won't. Assuming that literally every object has a spirit present to oversee it makes the setting fall apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119927#post1119927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The statement simply struck me as a bit odd to me in a setting in which people know that gods do exist (if you want to open a salt mine and you make the local salt gods mad they are going to kill you), in which people know gods can be killed (the fact that Immaculate Monks can fight and kill gods is no secret) and in which the largest religious order in the world makes it a point of fact that the sun had a god whom the Anathema stole their powers from. I would think much more likely that most people would simply assume that the Unconquered Sun is a dead god, probably killed by the Anathema, rather a god who never even existed in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of gods does not stop people from making up gods, any more than the existence of professionals prevents a person from making up doctors or scientists who conveniently agree with what they have to say.<br /> <br /> The existence of truth alone isn't enough to kill a lie; you have to be willing to apply scrutiny to what the liar is saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-24-2017, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:42:10-07:00","id":1119947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119236#post1119236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is one of those examples in which I think that this level of granularity doesn't really work. The Cult Merit is too straightforward, it doesn't accommodate questions of how it works when a certain subset of a Direction is especially dedicated compared to the more casual, even perfunctory worshippers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm just using it as a mental model of how the Sol, Luna, the Maidens and Gaia gets a boost even if not many are directly aware of them anymore. It will probably never directly affect a player character, so I don't have to bother with mechanics for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119236#post1119236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo from there I got the impression that worship of the Sun would fall out of fashion not because anybody specifically discouraged it, but as an emergent property of changes in the social context. Breakdowns in the Second Age changed the incentives behind why people worship in the first place, and alter the market of what gods are at work, and eventually you get a scenario in which worshipping the Sun is something that hardly anybody has the time or attention for. Eventually, the lack of reiterated attention means that you simply get generations of people who grow up with references to the Most High sun god being something they occasionally hear from their grandparents, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119875#post1119875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that that's the most plausible way to do it. When the Sun doesn't answer your prayers while the local forest goddess does (and sends wood spiders to attack your livestock if you don't pray to her), over time, people are just going to worship the Sun less and less.<br /> Plus, of course, the Immaculate Order gets upset over you worshipping local gods, but they get really upset over you worshipping the UCS.<br /> So... why bother.<br /> It's not that no-one <i>ever</i> worships him, there's probably small sun cults and so forth, it's just rare.<br /> <br /> And I'd guess forgotten means in the sense that maybe if you ask a scholar of religion, they might be able to tell you that the sun has a god called The Unconquered Sun, but your average peasant couldn't name him (whereas they probably could name the main gods worshipped by their culture, and some local terrestrial Gods). It's not that the idea of the Sun having a god is radically strange to them, it's just... well, who cares? It's not very important. He's the god of the sun, not the god of peasants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if there ever have existed a farmer that haven't obsessed with things like sun and rain. So probably the only reason a farmer would never praying for more or less or sun would be because we are talking about an atheist, and instead hoping for the physical forces that affects weather ends up favorable.<br /> <br /> Then, combine with the human trait of seeing patterns where there is none. So even if there is no response, quite a few would most likely still believe their prayers where heard.<br /> <br /> So while they might not pray to the entity &quot;The Uncured Sun&quot;, there are probably a lot of people sending prayers and offerings to that great ball of fire in the sky, maybe with a &quot;god&quot; someone made up a few generations back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:18:45-07:00","id":1119963,"title":"","content":"First, thank you to people that provided the information that confirmed that I was wrong about the Order's view towards the Sun! I looked up old 1e books even, and it's clear that the Usurpation not only involved the murder of the Solar Exalted, but the wholesale abolishment of the dominant world religion! Here is a relevant quote...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Unconquered Sun:</b> Mightiest among the gods, the Unconquered Sun was their leader when they rebelled against those who came before the gods. He created the Solar Exalted and advised them when they ruled the world during the First Age, until the Solars\u2019 overweening pride caused him to turn away from them. His temples were pulled down after the murder of the Solar Exalted, and his worship was banned. Today, the veneration of the Unconquered Sun is practiced only by savages and isolated bands of heretics. </div> </div> </div>So, proceeding from the premise that I know I was wrong according to the canon, I want to briefly discuss why I think this is really, really silly and poorly thought though.<br /> <br /> First, let's examine the political reality of the situation. The Usurpation itself is a hugely impacting event. It's gotta be shocking that the Solar Exalted were murdered, but maybe we can assume that'd not be overly chaotic because they'd already made such a scandalous reputation for themselves that more or less the population isn't that sad to see them go.<br /> <br /> But then we get into the widescale dismantling of the dominant faith of a quasi-modern mother society with population numbers in the BILLIONS and near universal acceptance of this faith. And, frankly, it becomes... difficult to envision success.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way - Let's say the Pope and all of his Cardinals are proven to be guilty of widespread and monstrous abuses. Let's even suggest the most favorable situation possible to the Usurpers and assume that knowledge of these crimes is widespread and commonly known. So not only is the Pope and all these high church officials guilty, everybody KNOWS they are guilty and is sick and tired of them.<br /> <br /> Under these circumstances it's perfectly reasonable and even perhaps desirable for an insurgent faction to remove these individuals and punish them on behalf of the people! But... can anybody honestly envision a situation where based on this, CHRISTIANITY AS A WHOLE would be dismantled? Keeping in mind that 99% of the population is devout Christian?<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the odds of even an ATTEMPT would be low... because it would be immediately seen as absurd! That is not how religion works! And even if such an attempt were made, it would be effectively impossible to succeed in any reasonable interpretation, and would almost certainly fail spectacularly.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm personally enamored with the idea that the Dragonblooded never forbade Sol worship. Why would they? They already have a stated position that the Solar Exalted are actually demon sorcerers who usurped power that didn't belong to them, so what is so bad about Sol worship that it needs to be abolished? The cost in political and social capital would have been immense for practically no benefit whatsoever.<br /> <br /> In addition, as other posters have pointed out better than me, the story of the Anathema relies upon the Celestial Gods as a key element. It seems counter intuitive to suppress knowledge of a key aspect state propaganda.<br /> <br /> I really think a more 'realistic' modern situation would have the entire Celestial Pantheon being worshiped, even perhaps given a festival day. All the better if the new Immaculate interpretations of these deities are interwoven culturally to the enshrined power structures of the Realm today - like for example, perhaps during the festival they have mockups of the Dragons and the Celestial Gods having tea together and reinforcing the idea of how good and perfect the Immaculate Order is.<br /> <br /> But of course, I do acknowledge I am completely wrong! After people corrected me here and got me digging at old books, I found that I was misinformed. I hope I've made a case for why I think my ideas weren't totally stupid however.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 07-24-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:30:25-07:00","id":1119967,"title":"","content":"While I didn't ead the whole discussion on this, I don't think it is that absurd to go and dismantle a Faith, even one as dominant as the UCS's when you have Fate Ninjas and Elemental Super heroes bearing down on it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say it happened overnight (I think, I haven't read the books). It might as well have taken centuries for it to be so largely forgotten. Add to that 2 cataclysmic events that, mathematically, decimated the population and the establishment of a NWO with a new religion you are oblkigated to follow and it is not that unimageniable to see how a once dominant religion has ceased to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:44:10-07:00","id":1119973,"title":"","content":"The erasure of whole 'faiths' (I'd hardly refer to the First Age worship of UCS as one religion, that is far far too unified for my taste on the First Age) isn't hard to imagine. Consider that the Immaculate Philosphy has a number of potential advantages:<br /> 1) It's evangelical. If UCS has a faith, and we consider the Dragon Kings an example of it, it comes off like most religions in creation do: Mostly a religion of ethnic/national locale, not one that seeks to spread itself over the world. This could be wrong, of course, but UCS faith always seemed more Zeus-y/Thor-y/Indra-y then YHWH. Or heck, YHWH but Old Testament-y.<br /> 2) The new leaders of the world are endorsed by it/endorse it. The Dragonblooded can cite immaculate (philosphical) doctrine for their revolt, and use it to back their own power. <br /> 3)The champions of said faith didn't mysteriously vanish, never to be seen for another thousand years.<br /> 4) It's got some genuinely good lifestyle advice in there, and has the odd distinction of being designed by humans, for humans, with little divine input. In fact, the Immaculate order operates against such input.<br /> 5) The UCS is tied to the First Age solars. Depending on your casting of the First Age, this might be enough to make people willing to jump ship to the other side (I run End Of First Age as an Age of Nightmares, so...yeah).<br /> <br /> I don't think in a VACUUM you'd see the Celestial worship vanish, but a concentrated effort to erradicate a faith over the years could do it pretty easily. Go ask the Gnostics, platonists, and mystery cultists of Greece.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:49:31-07:00","id":1119976,"title":"","content":"Well, we're not talking about Immaculates initially in any case (who knows what the early Shogunate faith was), but that distinction is kinda nitpicky and not that important to make. Your points are well taken.<br /> <br /> Answering the ideas put forward, I actually completely agree - I could see a faith vanishing in a century or two, sure. It's easy enough to create incentives that will move people from one way of thinking to another. In fact, I think if one is enamored with the idea of a 'Forgotten God' for pure story reasons or coolness, that's a pretty good way to do it. Just suggest that over time, sun worship became less and less important, until it more or less vanished into obscurity under the weight of an immense amount of theological focus and energy being devoted to separate areas.<br /> <br /> But the text describes actually PULLING DOWN THE TEMPLES - like, immediately as the Solar Exalted were killed.<br /> <br /> That's where I kinda go 'Waitaminute'.<br /> <br /> In order for that to really work, I find myself verging more into the 'Age of Nightmares' interpretation than I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:59:48-07:00","id":1119980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119976#post1119976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the text describes actually PULLING DOWN THE TEMPLES - like, immediately as the Solar Exalted were killed.<br /> <br /> That's where I kinda go 'Waitaminute'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, no, it explicitly says &quot;after&quot; <i>in the text you're quoting</i>. Don't know where you got &quot;as.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:07:44-07:00","id":1119985,"title":"","content":"Going by the text you quoted, it says &quot;...after the murder...&quot; so that may be a very long time. Even today (in Creation) it is still &quot;after the murder&quot;. And even today we still have standing, albeit abandoned, temples to the UCS. Which suggests the purge wasn't as complete, violent or symmetric as one would think.<br /> <br /> Since the process of said dismantling is not discussed in detail, we sholudn't take these genarilities to be too limiting or let them impose on our suspension of disbelief. If them going balls to the walls on the UCS Faith irks you, nothing you quoted contradicts assuming things were more gradual.<br /> <br /> I personally envision it as a &quot;The UCS is very angry with the state of the world. He doesn't want to be bothered by your prayers. We're closing this temple and you better start praying to gods who maybe will listen instead of one who said that he will smite those who bother him.&quot; Spectacularly kill some stubborn fools. Rinse and repeat through centuries. Introduce a new state religion with tremendous secular backing, and let the UCS fade into non existence.<br /> <br /> In this magical world people would notice that their god stopped answering. In this magical world you have the Princes of the Earth, nigh immortal super people, telling you whats up. Your beloved UCS is not raining down beams of searing light as they board up His temples and arrests unyielding believers. Some shit is certainly up with your God, so your best bet is get with the new program if you don't wanna go the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:30:23-07:00","id":1119999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119934#post1119934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, yeah, no, that's taking it too far. A blade of grass <i>might</i> have a spirit overseeing it (for example, a Censor could've punished a god by demoting it to some menial task), but it probably won't. Assuming that literally every object has a spirit present to oversee it makes the setting fall apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this break the setting? It's literally exactly how it worked in 2E:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Roll of Glorious Divinity 1 - Gods and Elementals pg 8</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods are omnipresent throughout Creation. The smallest stone and simplest tool each has its own least god. Through the least gods\u2019 interaction, they define Creation\u2019s natural law.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not gonna try to defend whether that's a good idea, but I will point out that the least gods were &quot;barely sentient&quot; if that makes it an easier pill to swallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:38:13-07:00","id":1120010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119976#post1119976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we're not talking about Immaculates initially in any case (who knows what the early Shogunate faith was), but that distinction is kinda nitpicky and not that important to make. Your points are well taken.<br /> <br /> Answering the ideas put forward, I actually completely agree - I could see a faith vanishing in a century or two, sure. It's easy enough to create incentives that will move people from one way of thinking to another. In fact, I think if one is enamored with the idea of a 'Forgotten God' for pure story reasons or coolness, that's a pretty good way to do it. Just suggest that over time, sun worship became less and less important, until it more or less vanished into obscurity under the weight of an immense amount of theological focus and energy being devoted to separate areas.<br /> <br /> But the text describes actually PULLING DOWN THE TEMPLES - like, immediately as the Solar Exalted were killed.<br /> <br /> That's where I kinda go 'Waitaminute'.<br /> <br /> In order for that to really work, I find myself verging more into the 'Age of Nightmares' interpretation than I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the key thing is that, even with temples pulled down, probably the religion didn't vanish within 10 years, 100 years, maybe even 1000 years.<br /> But it's 1500 years later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think of it this way - Let's say the Pope and all of his Cardinals are proven to be guilty of widespread and monstrous abuses. Let's even suggest the most favorable situation possible to the Usurpers and assume that knowledge of these crimes is widespread and commonly known. So not only is the Pope and all these high church officials guilty, everybody KNOWS they are guilty and is sick and tired of them.<br /> <br /> Under these circumstances it's perfectly reasonable and even perhaps desirable for an insurgent faction to remove these individuals and punish them on behalf of the people! But... can anybody honestly envision a situation where based on this, CHRISTIANITY AS A WHOLE would be dismantled? Keeping in mind that 99% of the population is devout Christian? </div> </div> </div>Consider that, in Western Europe, a mere 500 years after attempts to reform and revitalise, sparked by some corruption and social change... Christianity has gone from 99% to under 50%. And that's without (unlike Eastern Europe) overt attempts to suppress it. It's likely to fall to somewhere between 20-30% in the next 50 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> With 1500 years of social changes, deliberate attempts to suppress the religion by the DBs and Sidereals, and no answered prayers compared to all the Gods that do answer prayers... well, I wouldn't expect there to be no worship of the UCS, but not a lot.<br /> <br /> Though I could see some of this going on:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if there ever have existed a farmer that haven't obsessed with things like sun and rain.<br /> ...<br /> So while they might not pray to the entity &quot;The Uncured Sun&quot;, there are probably a lot of people sending prayers and offerings to that great ball of fire in the sky, maybe with a &quot;god&quot; someone made up a few generations back. </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:39:00-07:00","id":1120011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1119999#post1119999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this break the setting? It's literally exactly how it worked in 2E:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not gonna try to defend whether that's a good idea, but I will point out that the least gods were &quot;barely sentient&quot; if that makes it an easier pill to swallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was toned down a lot in Ex3. And the previous devs had spoken on it a bit. The physics of the world are no longer &quot;least god interactions&quot;, but just a function of reality.<br /> <br /> We even have a recent question on the Ask the Devs thread where Eric says the vagueness is on purpose, that STs sghould adjust to their liking. He cautions on taking the &quot;gods everywhere&quot; approach and says he personally sets the game where even certain towns or villages having a god is not a foregone conclusion. So definately moved away from &quot;you have angered the god of this sheet of paper, takes this papercut, you fool!&quot; territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:41:48-07:00","id":1120012,"title":"","content":"To address another false dichotomy:<br /> <br /> \u200bI would find that there is a distinct difference between people doubting the existence of one or more sun gods, and people doubting the existence of the kind of god that the Unconquered Sun is. Even as the Incarnae (who would be incredible compared to even the most powerful among the small gods) go, the Unconquered Sun is a few steps beyond.<br /> <br /> \u200bFamiliarity with gods in general might actually be the kind of thing that increases scepticism that anything like the Incarnae ever existed.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for demographics of belief systems in the United States, well, not to put too fine a point on that, I think a lot of that might have something to do with how the foundations of the country had significant input from religious fundamentalists fleeing persecution in their homelands. &quot;Sinners in the hands of an angry God&quot; is not exactly indicative of religious belief systems across the world, or throughout the vast gulf of history in which the United States was not a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:54:01-07:00","id":1120023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1120012#post1120012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address another false dichotomy:<br /> <br /> \u200bI would find that there is a distinct difference between people doubting the existence of one or more sun gods, and people doubting the existence of the kind of god that the Unconquered Sun is. Even as the Incarnae (who would be incredible compared to even the most powerful among the small gods) go, the Unconquered Sun is a few steps beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very good point.<br /> When the Zenith comes to town and preaches that the Unconquered Sun, God of the Sun, wants you to throw down the Immaculate Temples, become righteous heroes, treat each other well, etc, and in fact himself threw down the Demon-Kings of old by creating the Solars, it's not the fact that the sun has a god that people react to with scepticism.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure lots of places believe the Sun God is a giant dung beetle, or a charioteer, or a big bird, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T14:04:03-07:00","id":1120064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1120023#post1120023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is a very good point.<br /> When the Zenith comes to town and preaches that the Unconquered Sun, God of the Sun, wants you to throw down the Immaculate Temples, become righteous heroes, treat each other well, etc, and in fact himself threw down the Demon-Kings of old by creating the Solars, it's not the fact that the sun has a god that people react to with scepticism.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure lots of places believe the Sun God is a giant dung beetle, or a charioteer, or a big bird, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And even when he is adored, he may not be the King of the Gods in the local culture. For example, in Nekhmet, a homebrewed kingdom in my campaign, the people think that Sol is a very important god... As a warrior, as he is supposed to be a very powerful soldier, so, in their mythology, he is mostly adored and revered as the protector of the gods and Creations against the Wyld. The Elemental Dragons are supposed to be the rulers of Creation, and he is nothing but their most loyal vassal. He wasn\u00b4t even a part of the original mythology, but when barbarians which adored him conquered the kingdom and assimilated into the local culture, they... inserted him into the local mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:29:57-07:00","id":1120101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1120011#post1120011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was toned down a lot in Ex3. And the previous devs had spoken on it a bit. The physics of the world are no longer &quot;least god interactions&quot;, but just a function of reality.<br /> <br /> We even have a recent question on the Ask the Devs thread where Eric says the vagueness is on purpose, that STs sghould adjust to their liking. He cautions on taking the &quot;gods everywhere&quot; approach and says he personally sets the game where even certain towns or villages having a god is not a foregone conclusion. So definately moved away from &quot;you have angered the god of this sheet of paper, takes this papercut, you fool!&quot; territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know, it just seemed like TheCountAlucard was laboring under a misapprehension re: 2E.<br /> <br /> I'm all for tossing the least gods idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:56:26-07:00","id":1120142,"title":"","content":"This thread is really making me consider the 'Lesser Sun Court', that is to say, spirits that handle sunly shit that aren't exactly the UCS himself.<br /> <br /> You'd figure such spirits gotta exist, right? So why haven't we heard about them? Primarily because it's confusing in terms of presentation to have to explain, 'Oh, but they have MANY sun Gods, not just one'. Which I can get!<br /> <br /> But... let's forego simplicity for a second and get ridiculously over complicated and speculate!<br /> <br /> Wouldn't a Southern Sun be cool? A Northern Sun? I bet each of these spirits could have a very unique character tied to the lore of those directions. And what about Aspect spirits? Spirits of the Dawn, spirits of the Twilight? Or personified spirits of benign intention of malice? Crop-bringer or head-roaster?<br /> <br /> And I'd imagine the Golden Lord is in there somewhere, too! Couldn't he be a sun spirit of war?<br /> <br /> In any event, I rather think Creation should be littered with Sun Gods - I don't think the UCS should have full thematic dominion over this one aspect of spiritual power.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:18:16-07:00","id":1120155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1120142#post1120142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is really making me consider the 'Lesser Sun Court', that is to say, spirits that handle sunly shit that aren't exactly the UCS himself.<br /> <br /> You'd figure such spirits gotta exist, right? So why haven't we heard about them? Primarily because it's confusing in terms of presentation to have to explain, 'Oh, but they have MANY sun Gods, not just one'. Which I can get!<br /> <br /> But... let's forego simplicity for a second and get ridiculously over complicated and speculate!<br /> <br /> Wouldn't a Southern Sun be cool? A Northern Sun? I bet each of these spirits could have a very unique character tied to the lore of those directions. And what about Aspect spirits? Spirits of the Dawn, spirits of the Twilight? Or personified spirits of benign intention of malice? Crop-bringer or head-roaster?<br /> <br /> And I'd imagine the Golden Lord is in there somewhere, too! Couldn't he be a sun spirit of war?<br /> <br /> In any event, I rather think Creation should be littered with Sun Gods - I don't think the UCS should have full thematic dominion over this one aspect of spiritual power.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could fit with the meso-American &quot;the sun is a role, not a person&quot; with Conkey specifically being the only sun that was unconquered, rather than THE sun who is also unconquered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T15:32:58-07:00","id":1122821,"title":"","content":"This is what we have in canon, quoting myself from page 6.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1114985-99-solar-pcs-are-muslim-kenyan-gay-atheist-commie?p=1116963#post1116963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're only mentioned in passing so we don't know much about them.<br /> Glories Luna page 14 mentions the god of Eclipses born of a union between The Unconquered Sun and Luna.<br /> Compass Yu-Shan page 44 mentions &quot;Thelmarin, Eastern Goddess of Peace and Twilight&quot;<br /> <br /> Not a sun god, but also in Yu-Shan is Sano-Medaro a Lesser Elemental Dragon in the Bureau of Nature with the title &quot;Daimyo of Sunshine&quot; a position which probably also takes its cut of prayer directed to the sun as celestial object associated with good weather.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that the Compass of Terrestrial Directions books helped to marginalise spirits that weren't included in them in the eyes of the fanbase then Compass Yu-Shan was utterly uninspiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:08:52-07:00","id":1124910,"title":"","content":"As I see it, least gods both are and are not a thing, mostly not. Everything in Creation has a spiritual presence, sometimes called a &quot;least god,&quot; but this term is misleading, in that a &quot;god&quot; must have at least some slight awareness to actually be a god, and the overwhelmingly majority of things simply do not have awareness. A beach might have a god, a mountain or a field might have one, but an individual grain, or even a large sack, of rice will not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}